(function(global){
'use strict';
const RA=global.RA=global.RA||{};
const D=(w,p)=>RA.D(w,p);
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({wrong,right,reason,errorType});
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('virus','Virus comes from Latin virus, “poison” or “toxic fluid”; modern biology uses it for an infectious agent, and computing borrowed the name for destructive self-copying software.',[C('virus.s1','biology','The virus can reproduce only inside living cells, so the researchers grew it in a controlled culture.','这种病毒只能在活细胞内复制，因此研究人员在受控培养环境中培育它。','infectious virus; virus infects cells','极小的感染性因子，只有在活细胞内才能繁殖。','The agent depends on living cells to reproduce.','病毒'),C('virus.s2','computing','A computer virus copied itself to shared files and damaged the office network.','电脑病毒把自身复制到共享文件中，并破坏了办公室网络。','computer virus; detect/remove a virus','指会自我复制并损坏数据或系统的隐藏程序。','The software copies itself and causes damage.','计算机病毒')],M('The computer virus protected every file and stopped itself from copying.','The computer virus damaged files and copied itself to other folders.','A computer virus is known for copying itself and causing damage.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where can the biological virus reproduce?','Inside living cells','On a dry desk by itself','Only inside a computer','Sense 1 describes an infectious agent dependent on living cells.','meaning'),Q(2,'What did the computer virus do?','Copied itself and damaged shared files','Repaired every document','Improved the network speed','Sense 2 is malicious self-copying software.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a computer virus','a viral computer-virusly','a virus of computerly','Virus is a count noun in this use.','grammar'),Q(2,'Why is computer malware called a virus?','It can copy itself and spread','It is made of living cells','It always improves data','The computing sense borrows the idea of replication and spread.','word-formation')]);
P('visa','Visa is from Latin charta visa, “paper that has been seen,” through European legal usage; it names entry permission and can also mean stamp that permission in a passport.',[C('visa.s1','travel','Her student visa allows her to stay in Canada for the length of her course.','她的学生签证允许她在课程期间留在加拿大。','apply for/get a visa; visa requirements','护照上的官方许可，准许入境、离境或停留。','The document authorizes her stay.','签证'),C('visa.s2','administration','The consulate will visa the passport after approving the application.','申请获批后，领事馆会在护照上签注。','visa a passport; visa a document','作动词，指把签证或许可正式签注在护照上。','The office records the permission in the passport.','签注')],M('She visaed the passport by taking the entry permit out of it and destroying it.','She had the passport visaed by having the consulate stamp the approved permit in it.','To visa a passport is to endorse it with a permit, not remove the permit.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does her student visa allow?','A permitted stay during her course','A degree without study','Automatic citizenship','Sense 1 is official travel or stay permission.','context'),Q(2,'What will the consulate do to the passport?','Stamp the approved permission in it','Take the passport apart','Cancel every visa worldwide','Sense 2 uses visa as a verb for endorsing a passport.','context'),Q(1,'Which collocation is standard?','apply for a visa','apply a visa to travel for','visa an application for','A traveler applies for the permission document.','collocation'),Q(2,'In “the office will visa the passport,” visa is…','a verb meaning endorse it with a permit','a noun meaning a country','an adjective describing paper','The source also records a transitive verb sense.','grammar')]);
P('viscera','Viscera is the plural of Latin viscus, “internal organ,” and collectively names soft organs inside the body.',C('viscera.s1','anatomy','The anatomy lesson identified the viscera, including the intestines and other soft internal organs.','解剖课辨认了内脏，包括肠道和其他柔软的内部器官。','internal viscera; abdominal viscera','名词复数，统称肠道等柔软的内部器官。','The organs lie inside the body.','内脏'),M('The surgeon examined the viscera, meaning the bones and hair on the outside of the body.','The surgeon examined the viscera, meaning the soft internal organs.','Viscera means internal organs, not external hair or bones.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does viscera refer to?','Soft internal organs','The outer layer of skin only','The bones of the fingers','The plural noun collectively names inner organs.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which items were named in the lesson?','Intestines and other inner organs','Shoelaces and buttons','Leaves and roots','The context gives examples of viscera.','context'),Q(1,'Viscera is grammatically…','a plural collective noun','the singular of a verb','an adjective meaning visible','The word is the plural form of Latin viscus.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which adjective naturally modifies viscera?','internal','wooden','electrical','Viscera are organs inside the body.','collocation')]);
P('viscosity','Viscosity is formed from viscous + -ity and names a fluid’s resistance to flowing.',C('viscosity.s1','physics','The high viscosity of cold honey makes it pour much more slowly than water.','冷蜂蜜黏度很高，因此比水流得慢得多。','fluid viscosity; measure viscosity','名词，指液体抵抗流动的程度。','The honey resists flowing.','黏度'),M('The water had high viscosity because it ran through the pipe faster than honey.','The honey had high viscosity because it ran through the pipe more slowly than water.','Slow flow indicates greater viscosity than water’s rapid flow.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why does cold honey pour slowly?','Its viscosity is high','Its temperature is above boiling','It has no mass','Viscosity measures resistance to flowing.','context'),Q(1,'A fluid with high viscosity…','resists flowing','flows as quickly as possible','cannot be measured','The definition concerns how readily fluid moves.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which word names the property?','viscosity','viscous','viscously','The suffix -ity turns viscous into a noun for a property.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which comparison follows the context?','Cold honey flows more slowly than water','Water has greater viscosity because it flows faster','Honey has no resistance to flow','The example links greater viscosity to slower flow.','context')]);
P('viscous','Viscous comes from Latin viscosus, “sticky,” and describes a thick fluid that flows slowly.',C('viscous.s1','materials','The viscous tar crept down the roof only a few centimeters during the cold night.','寒冷的夜里，黏稠的焦油沿屋顶只流下了几厘米。','viscous fluid/liquid; thick and viscous','形容液体浓稠黏滞、流动缓慢。','The tar moves only slowly.','黏稠的'),M('The viscous syrup splashed across the counter as quickly as water.','The thin syrup splashed across the counter as quickly as water.','A fluid that flows like water is not thick and viscous.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the tar move?','Slowly down the roof','Instantly across the whole roof','Upward into the sky','Viscous describes slow-flowing thickness.','context'),Q(1,'Honey is viscous when it…','is thick and flows slowly','is a thin gas','has no resistance to flow','The adjective describes thickness and slow movement.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a viscous liquid','a viscosity liquid','viscously liquid','Viscous is the adjective modifying liquid.','grammar'),Q(1,'The Latin source viscosus means…','sticky','bright','empty','The word descends from a Latin term for sticky.','word-formation')]);
P('vise','Vise comes through French vis, “screw,” and names a tool whose jaws hold material firmly for cutting or shaping.',C('vise.s1','workshop','Clamp the wooden block in the vise before drilling so it cannot slip.','钻孔前把木块夹在台钳里，免得它滑动。','bench vise; clamp something in a vise','名词，指用两片钳口夹牢木料或金属的工具。','The jaws secure the workpiece.','台钳'),M('He secured the metal in the vise by leaving the jaws wide open around it.','He secured the metal in the vise by tightening the jaws around it.','Open jaws cannot hold the workpiece firmly.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why clamp the wood in a vise?','To keep it from slipping while drilling','To paint it without touching it','To measure its temperature','A vise holds a workpiece securely.','context'),Q(1,'What part grips the material?','The vise’s jaws','Its electric cord','A measuring scale','The two jaws close on the workpiece.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','clamp the block in a vise','clamp the block at vise it','vise the block into clamping','The normal construction is clamp something in a vise.','grammar'),Q(1,'The word vise is historically related to French…','vis, “screw”','vue, “view”','vie, “life”','The tool uses a screw mechanism to close its jaws.','word-formation')]);
P('visibility','Visibility comes from visible + -ity and means how clearly something can be seen or how widely it is noticed.',[C('visibility.s1','weather','Fog reduced visibility on the highway, so drivers slowed down and switched on their lights.','大雾降低了高速公路上的能见度，因此司机减速并打开车灯。','poor/good visibility; visibility is reduced','指受光线、雾或黑暗影响的可见距离或清晰度。','Drivers cannot see far ahead.','能见度'),C('visibility.s2','publicity','The museum’s new website increased the visibility of its smaller local-history exhibits.','博物馆的新网站提高了其小型地方史展品的公众关注度。','public/media visibility; gain visibility','指某人或事物被公众知晓、注意的程度。','More people notice the exhibits.','公众关注度')],M('Fog improved visibility because drivers could see less than one meter ahead.','Fog reduced visibility because drivers could see less than one meter ahead.','Seeing less means visibility is reduced, not improved.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did drivers slow down?','Fog reduced how clearly they could see','The road was completely dry','Their cars had no brakes','Sense 1 concerns visual clarity and distance.','context'),Q(2,'What did the new website increase?','Public notice of the local-history exhibits','The size of the museum building','The fog outside','Sense 2 is how widely something is noticed.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','poor visibility in fog','visibility poorly in fog','fog visibilityly poor','Visibility is a noun modified by poor.','grammar'),Q(2,'A local artist seeking visibility wants…','more people to notice their work','a darker room','less public attention','The public sense concerns being seen or noticed.','meaning')]);
P('visible','Visible comes from Latin visibilis, “able to be seen,” from videre, “see”; it can also mean clear enough to be noticed.',[C('visible.s1','sight','The red warning light is visible from the entrance, even in daylight.','即使在白天，从入口处也能看见红色警示灯。','clearly/easily visible; visible to the eye','形容词，指眼睛能够看到的。','The light can be seen at a distance.','看得见的'),C('visible.s2','notice','The impact of the repair was visible in the lower number of complaints.','投诉数量减少，维修效果显而易见。','visible effect/change; become visible','指清楚到足以引起注意的。','The result is noticeable in the figures.','明显的')],M('The visible warning light could not be seen from the entrance even in daylight.','The invisible warning light could not be seen from the entrance even in daylight.','If it cannot be seen, it is not visible.','meaning'),[Q(1,'From where is the warning light visible?','From the entrance','Only from inside the lamp','Nowhere in daylight','Sense 1 means able to be seen.','context'),Q(2,'How was the repair’s impact visible?','Complaints became fewer','The roof changed color only','The repair remained secret','Sense 2 is a noticeable result.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','visible to the eye','visible for the eye','visibly to an eye','The usual phrase is visible to someone or visible to the eye.','grammar'),Q(1,'Visible traces to Latin videre, meaning…','to see','to speak','to carry','Its history is tied to seeing.','word-formation')]);
P('vision','Vision comes from Latin visio, “act of seeing,” from videre; it means eyesight, a guiding idea for the future, or an imagined sight.',[C('vision.s1','health','The eye test showed that his vision had improved after he got new glasses.','验光显示，戴上新眼镜后他的视力有所改善。','clear/poor vision; field of vision','名词，指看见事物的能力。','The test measures eyesight.','视力'),C('vision.s2','leadership','The director’s vision is to make the library a welcoming center for every neighborhood.','馆长的愿景是让图书馆成为每个社区都乐于使用的中心。','a vision for the future; share a vision','名词，指对未来的清晰构想。','The director describes a future goal.','愿景'),C('vision.s3','dream','As she woke, she remembered a vivid vision of a city floating above the sea.','醒来时，她记得一个生动的幻象：一座城市漂浮在海面上方。','a vision in a dream; have a vision','名词，指梦境或想象中仿佛看见的事物。','The city was imagined, not physically present.','幻象')],M('The eye doctor said his vision improved, meaning he became unable to see any letters.','The eye doctor said his vision worsened, meaning he became unable to see any letters.','Improved vision means better sight, not losing the ability to read.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What improved after the new glasses?','His eyesight','The library’s future plan','A dream city','Sense 1 means the ability to see.','context'),Q(2,'What is the director’s vision?','A future library serving every neighborhood','A past meeting record','A pair of glasses','Sense 2 is a guiding future idea.','context'),Q(3,'Where did the floating city appear?','In a remembered dreamlike image','On an actual map at the library','In the eye-test chart','Sense 3 is an imagined or dream sight.','context'),Q(1,'Vision comes from a Latin word meaning…','seeing','building','hearing','The root is related to the act of seeing.','word-formation')]);
P('visional','Visional is a rare adjective formed from vision + -al, describing eyesight or something dreamlike and unreal.',C('visional.s1','literature','The poet describes a visional landscape that seems to appear in a dream rather than in the real world.','诗人描绘了一幅仿佛出现在梦中、而非现实世界的幻景。','visional image/landscape; dreamlike and visional','罕见形容词，指与视觉有关或带有梦幻、不真实色彩。','The landscape is presented as dreamlike imagery.','幻景的'),M('The visional landscape was a solid hill that hikers could touch and measure.','The real landscape was a solid hill that hikers could touch and measure.','A tangible measured hill is real, not dreamlike and visional.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How does the poem present the landscape?','As a dreamlike image','As a measured highway','As a chemical solution','Visional can describe something dreamlike or unreal.','context'),Q(1,'Visional is…','a rare adjective related to vision','a common word for a visitor','a noun for a passport','The source entry labels it an adjective.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits the source sense?','a visional image','a visional passport stamp','a visional screwdriver','The word relates to sight or dreamlike imagery.','collocation'),Q(1,'The suffix -al commonly forms…','an adjective','a plural noun','a past-tense verb','Visional is an adjective from vision + -al.','word-formation')]);
P('visit','Visit comes from Latin visitare, “go to see”; it can mean see a person/place, view a website or stay briefly, or the occasion itself.',[C('visit.s1','social','We visit our grandparents every Sunday and stay for lunch.','我们每周日都去看望祖父母，并在那里吃午饭。','visit a person/place; pay someone a visit','去看望某人或参观某地并停留一段时间。','The family goes to see relatives.','探望'),C('visit.s2','online','Thousands of readers visit the archive website to search old newspapers.','成千上万的读者访问档案网站，搜索旧报纸。','visit a website/page; website visits','访问网站或短暂停留在某处。','Readers open and use the website.','访问'),C('visit.s3','occasion','Our last visit to the science museum lasted three hours.','我们上次参观科学博物馆持续了三个小时。','pay a visit; a brief/long visit','名词，指去看望或参观的一次活动。','It names the occasion, not the act alone.','拜访/参观')],M('We visited the museum by refusing to enter it or look at anything inside.','We visited the museum by going inside and looking at its exhibits.','A visit to a museum involves going there, not refusing to enter.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What do they do on Sundays?','See their grandparents and eat lunch','Search the archive website','Take a science exam','Sense 1 is going to see a person.','context'),Q(2,'Why do readers visit the archive site?','To search old newspapers','To visit the grandparents in person','To repair the server','Sense 2 means go to or use a website.','context'),Q(3,'What lasted three hours?','Their museum visit','A website password','A weekly lunch recipe','Sense 3 is the occasion of visiting.','context'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses visit as a noun?','Our visit lasted three hours.','We visit every Sunday.','They visit the website.','In the first sentence, visit is an occasion noun.','grammar')]);
P('visitor','Visitor is formed from visit + -or and names a guest, a tourist, or a temporary organism in a place.',[C('visitor.s1','home','Please leave your coat by the door; our next visitor is arriving at six.','请把外套放在门边；下一位来访者六点到。','welcome/receive a visitor; visitor to a home','短时间来访的人。','The person comes to see the household.','来访者'),C('visitor.s2','tourism','Each visitor to the national park receives a map at the entrance.','每位到国家公园游览的游客都会在入口处领到地图。','park/museum visitor; visitor attraction','参观景点的游客，常指一日游或度假者。','The people are visiting a place of interest.','游客'),C('visitor.s3','ecology','The island’s rare plants are threatened by a visitor species brought in on cargo ships.','货船带来的外来物种威胁着岛上的稀有植物。','migrant/temporary visitor; visitor species','指暂时到某地停留后会离开的生物或事物。','The organism is not permanently established there.','暂居生物')],M('The park visitor stayed at home all day and never entered the park.','The park visitor entered the park to see its trails and wildlife.','Someone who never goes to the park is not a visitor there.','meaning'),[Q(1,'When will the next visitor arrive?','At six','On the cargo ship next year','After the map is printed','Sense 1 is a person coming to someone’s home.','context'),Q(2,'What does each national-park visitor receive?','A map at the entrance','A visitor species','A passport visa','Sense 2 is a tourist at an attraction.','context'),Q(3,'What threatens the island plants?','A species temporarily brought in by ships','A permanent native tree','A park map','Sense 3 describes a temporary organism.','context'),Q(1,'Visitor is formed from…','visit + -or, a person or thing that visits','vision + -al','vocal + -ist','The suffix -or forms an agent noun from visit.','word-formation')]);
P('visor','Visor comes from a word for seeing or looking and names either a protective face screen on a helmet or a sun-shield above a vehicle windscreen.',[C('visor.s1','protective gear','The rider lowered her helmet visor before starting the motorcycle.','骑手启动摩托车前放下了头盔面罩。','helmet visor; lower/raise a visor','固定在头盔上的金属或塑料挡片，保护面部并留有视线开口。','The visor shields her face while she can still see.','面罩'),C('visor.s2','car','I pulled down the car visor to keep the low afternoon sun out of my eyes.','我把汽车遮阳板拉下来，挡住下午刺眼的低角度阳光。','sun visor; pull down the visor','汽车挡风玻璃上方可拉下的遮阳板。','The panel blocks sunlight from the driver’s eyes.','遮阳板')],M('She lowered the helmet visor so the wind and insects could hit her face directly.','She raised the helmet visor so the wind and insects could hit her face directly.','Lowering a visor protects the face; raising it exposes the face.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the rider lower?','The protective screen on her helmet','The motorcycle’s rear wheel','A passport page','Sense 1 is a face-protecting helmet part.','context'),Q(2,'Why pull down a car visor?','To block low sun from the driver’s eyes','To cover the license plate','To open the window','Sense 2 is the vehicle’s sun-shield panel.','context'),Q(1,'Which compound is standard?','sun visor','sun visor of the helmet only','visor sunning','The car accessory is commonly called a sun visor.','collocation'),Q(1,'Both senses of visor protect…','the face or eyes while allowing sight','the engine from rain','a passport from water','The two source senses shield a person’s face or eyes.','meaning')]);
P('vista','Vista comes from Italian vista, “view,” from vedere, “to see”; it means a long attractive view or a range of new possibilities.',[C('vista.s1','landscape','From the tower, a long vista of vineyards stretched toward the distant hills.','从塔上望去，一片葡萄园景色延伸至远处的山丘。','a magnificent vista; open up a vista','长而优美的景色，常从开口或建筑之间望见。','The view extends far into the distance.','远景'),C('vista.s2','possibilities','The scholarship opened a vista of new career possibilities for the first-generation student.','奖学金为这名第一代大学生打开了新的职业前景。','a vista of possibilities/opportunities; open up vistas','比喻新的可能性或经历。','The scholarship makes new paths available.','前景')],M('The scholarship opened a vista of possibilities by closing every career path to her.','The scholarship opened a vista of possibilities by giving her new career paths.','A vista of possibilities means new paths open, not all paths close.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the tower overlook?','A long view of vineyards and hills','A single indoor desk','A short tunnel','Sense 1 is an attractive long view.','context'),Q(2,'What did the scholarship open?','New career possibilities','A window in the tower','A closed road','Sense 2 is figurative new opportunity.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a vista of possibilities','a vista to possible','a possible vista of to','The idiom uses vista of + possibilities.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vista is historically linked to Italian…','vista, “view”','vita, “life”','viscera, “organs”','The word comes from an Italian term for a view.','word-formation')]);
P('visual','Visual comes from Latin visualis, from videre, “see”; it describes sight or names an explanatory picture, chart, or film.',[C('visual.s1','perception','The visual contrast between the dark text and pale background makes the warning easy to read.','深色文字与浅色背景之间的视觉对比让警告易于阅读。','visual effect/detail; visual contrast','形容词，指与视觉或眼睛有关。','The contrast is perceived by sight.','视觉的'),C('visual.s2','teaching','The teacher used a simple visual to show how the water cycle works.','老师用一张简单图示说明水循环的过程。','use/show a visual; visual aid','名词，指用于解释信息的图片、图表或影片。','The diagram explains the process.','图示')],M('The visual diagram helped students understand the cycle without showing them any picture or chart.','The verbal explanation helped students understand the cycle without showing them any picture or chart.','A visual is a picture or chart; a purely spoken explanation is verbal.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What made the warning easy to read?','Its strong visual contrast','Its loud sound','Its fragrance','Sense 1 relates to seeing.','context'),Q(2,'What did the teacher use?','A diagram explaining the water cycle','A spoken-only instruction','A bottle of water','Sense 2 is an explanatory picture or chart.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses visual as an adjective?','visual contrast','a visual on the screen','two visuals','The first phrase uses visual to modify contrast.','grammar'),Q(2,'A visual in a lesson is…','a picture or chart used to explain','a student who sees the board','an audio recording only','The noun sense names explanatory media.','meaning')]);
P('visualise','Visualise is the British spelling of visualize, from visual + -ise; it means form a mental picture or turn information into a graphic.',[C('visualise.s1','planning','Before the interview, she visualised herself answering each difficult question calmly.','面试前，她想象自己从容回答每个棘手问题。','visualise a scene/future; mentally visualise','在头脑中形成清晰画面或设想。','She creates a mental picture before the event.','想象'),C('visualise.s2','data','The analyst visualised the survey results in a chart so the trend was easy to compare.','分析师把调查结果做成图表，便于比较趋势。','visualise data/results; visualise as a chart','把数据或想法用图片或图表呈现。','The chart makes the results visible.','可视化')],M('She visualised the survey results by hiding every chart and leaving the figures unreadable.','She obscured the survey results by hiding every chart and leaving the figures unreadable.','Visualising results makes them easier to see, not harder.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did she visualise before the interview?','Answering difficult questions calmly','The survey chart','A physical passport','Sense 1 means form a mental picture.','context'),Q(2,'How did the analyst visualise survey results?','By displaying them in a chart','By deleting the figures','By speaking without data','Sense 2 means present information graphically.','context'),Q(1,'Which spelling is standard in British English?','visualise','visualize','visualyze','Visualise is the British -ise spelling.','spelling'),Q(1,'Visualise is built from…','visual + -ise','visit + -or','vital + -ity','The verb means make visual or form a visual image.','word-formation')]);
P('visualize','Visualize is the American spelling of visualise, from visual + -ize; it means mentally picture something or show data graphically.',[C('visualize.s1','mental rehearsal','The climber visualized each step of the route before setting out at dawn.','登山者黎明出发前想象了路线上的每一步。','visualize a goal/scene; mentally visualize','在事情发生前于脑海中形成清晰画面。','The route is pictured mentally in advance.','想象'),C('visualize.s2','data','The team visualized monthly sales as a line graph to reveal the seasonal pattern.','团队用折线图呈现月销售额，以显示季节性规律。','visualize data/information; visualize as a graph','把信息或想法制成图表或图像。','A graph makes the pattern visible.','可视化')],M('The team visualized sales data by removing the graph and concealing the pattern.','The team obscured sales data by removing the graph and concealing the pattern.','A visualization reveals a pattern rather than concealing it.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the climber picture mentally?','Each step of the route','A monthly sales graph','A passport stamp','Sense 1 is mental imagery before an event.','context'),Q(2,'What did the line graph show?','The seasonal sales pattern','A mountain route','A visa expiration date','Sense 2 is graphical presentation of information.','context'),Q(1,'Which spelling is standard in American English?','visualize','visualise','visulize','Visualize is the American -ize spelling.','spelling'),Q(1,'Visualize is closest to…','form a mental image or make a visual display','visit a place briefly','measure voltage','The verb has mental and data-display uses.','meaning')]);
P('visually','Visually is formed from visual + -ly and means with respect to appearance or sight.',C('visually.s1','design','The two labels are visually distinct because one is blue and the other is bright yellow.','两个标签在视觉上很容易区分，因为一个是蓝色，另一个是亮黄色。','visually clear/distinct; visually inspect','副词，指就外观或视觉而言。','Their colors let the eye distinguish them.','视觉上'),M('The labels were visually distinct, though they looked exactly the same in color and shape.','The labels were visually identical, because their color and shape matched.','If color and shape match, they are not visually distinct.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why were the labels visually distinct?','Their colors differed clearly','They had no visible color','They were identical in every way','The difference is apparent to sight.','context'),Q(1,'Visually means…','with respect to appearance or sight','by sound alone','at a particular time','The adverb describes visual appearance.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','visually inspect the surface','visual inspect the surface','inspect visuallyly the surface','The adverb modifies inspect.','grammar'),Q(1,'The suffix -ly changes visual into…','an adverb','a plural noun','a past-tense verb','Visually tells how an action is done or judged.','word-formation')]);
P('vital','Vital comes from Latin vitalis, from vita, “life”; it means absolutely necessary or connected with life and energy.',[C('vital.s1','importance','A reliable map is vital to the rescue team searching the remote valley.','可靠的地图对搜寻偏远山谷的救援队至关重要。','vital to/for success; absolutely vital','形容词，指成功或生存所绝对必需。','Without the map the team cannot search effectively.','至关重要'),C('vital.s2','health','The nurse checked his vital signs and found that his breathing was steady.','护士检查了他的生命体征，发现呼吸平稳。','vital signs; vital organs','指与维持生命有关的，或充满生命力的。','Breathing and other signs indicate life functions.','生命的')],M('A map is vital to the rescue, but the team can search just as well without one.','A map is helpful but not vital to the rescue if the team can search without it.','Vital means absolutely necessary, while something optional is merely helpful.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why is a map vital to the rescue?','It is absolutely necessary for the search','It decorates the team’s office','It records the weather last year','Sense 1 means essential.','context'),Q(2,'What are vital signs?','Measurements of basic life functions','The team’s map symbols','A list of job titles','Sense 2 concerns signs connected with staying alive.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is standard?','vital to success','vital for succeeding to','vital at successly','Vital is commonly followed by to or for.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vital traces to Latin vita, meaning…','life','sight','voice','Its origin is the Latin word for life.','word-formation')]);
P('vitalism','Vitalism is formed from vital + -ism and names the theory that living things require a special force beyond physical laws.',C('vitalism.s1','philosophy','The history class contrasted vitalism with explanations that account for life through chemistry and physics alone.','历史课将活力论与仅用化学和物理解释生命的观点作了对比。','the theory of vitalism; vitalism in biology','名词，指生命受一种不能还原为物理规律的特殊生命力支配的学说。','The theory posits an extra vital force.','活力论'),M('Vitalism claims that living things are governed only by ordinary physical laws and no special life force.','Mechanistic theory claims that living things are governed only by ordinary physical laws and no special life force.','Vitalism specifically posits a special vital force beyond physical laws.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does vitalism posit?','A special life force beyond physical laws','That life has no relation to nature','That all living cells are machines with no theory','The source definition centers on an irreducible vital force.','meaning'),Q(1,'What did the class contrast with vitalism?','Explanations based only on chemistry and physics','A study of visa documents','A map of a valley','Vitalism is contrasted with purely physical explanations.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','the theory of vitalism','vitalismly theory','the vitalism to theory','Vitalism is a noun naming a theory.','grammar'),Q(1,'The suffix -ism often marks…','a doctrine or system of belief','a person who visits','a measurement unit','Vitalism names a philosophical doctrine.','word-formation')]);
P('vitalist','Vitalist is formed from vital + -ist and names an adherent of vitalism, the theory of a distinct life force.',C('vitalist.s1','philosophy','The vitalist argued that a living organism could not be fully explained by chemistry and physics alone.','这位活力论者认为，单靠化学和物理学无法充分解释生命体。','vitalist philosopher; vitalist theory','名词，指相信生命需要特殊非物质力量的人。','The speaker defends vitalism’s extra life principle.','活力论者'),M('The vitalist rejected vitalism and insisted that life depends on no special life force.','The mechanist rejected vitalism and insisted that life depends on no special life force.','Rejecting the vital force theory describes a mechanist, not a vitalist.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the vitalist argue?','Life cannot be fully explained by chemistry and physics alone','A living thing is exactly the same as a mineral','A visa is a life force','The vitalist supports a special principle of life.','context'),Q(1,'A vitalist is…','a person who holds vitalism','a person who measures voltage','a person who visits a museum','The -ist suffix marks an adherent of a doctrine.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','a vitalist philosopher','a vitalistly philosopher','a philosopher vitalismist','Vitalist is a noun modifying or identifying the philosopher.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vitalist is formed from…','vital + -ist','vitality + -ly','visitor + -or','The suffix names a person who holds the vitalist view.','word-formation')]);
P('vitality','Vitality is formed from vital + -ity and means energetic liveliness or the natural power to survive and grow.',[C('vitality.s1','energy','Despite the long journey, the dancer spoke with remarkable vitality and kept the children laughing.','尽管旅途漫长，舞者仍精力充沛地说笑，逗得孩子们开心。','energy and vitality; full of vitality','指充满精力、热情与活力的状态。','The dancer remains lively and energetic.','活力'),C('vitality.s2','biology','Healthy soil supports the vitality of young trees and helps them survive dry summers.','健康的土壤有助于幼树保持生命力，熬过干燥的夏季。','vitality of a species/plant; maintain vitality','指生物存活、成长和保持健康的自然能力。','The soil helps the trees grow and survive.','生命力')],M('The dancer showed vitality by sitting motionless, exhausted, and unable to speak.','The dancer showed fatigue by sitting motionless, exhausted, and unable to speak.','Exhaustion and immobility indicate low vitality.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the dancer’s vitality look like?','Energy and lively conversation','Inability to speak','A dry tree root','Sense 1 means energetic liveliness.','context'),Q(2,'How does healthy soil help young trees?','It supports their ability to grow and survive','It makes them forget how to grow','It changes them into dancers','Sense 2 concerns biological life and growth.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','full of vitality','full of vitalitiesly','vitality to energetic','The common phrase is full of vitality.','collocation'),Q(1,'Vitality names…','the quality or power of being alive and energetic','an official travel document','a tool that clamps wood','The noun comes from vital and covers energy or life force.','meaning')]);
P('vitamin','Vitamin is a coined scientific term from vita, “life,” and amine, an early chemical classification; it names essential nutrients or a supplement containing them.',[C('vitamin.s1','nutrition','The diet includes enough vitamin C to support normal tissue repair.','这种饮食含有足够的维生素C，有助于正常组织修复。','vitamin C/D; rich in vitamins','名词，指身体少量必需的营养物质。','The nutrient is present in food in a small amount.','维生素'),C('vitamin.s2','supplements','She takes a vitamin each morning because her doctor recommended a supplement.','她每天早晨服用一粒维生素补充剂，这是医生的建议。','take a vitamin; vitamin pill/drop','口语中也指含有维生素的药片或滴剂。','Here the word names a supplement product.','维生素补充剂')],M('She took a vitamin supplement as a replacement for every meal and all medical advice.','She took a vitamin supplement in addition to a balanced diet and medical advice.','A vitamin supplements a diet; it does not replace every meal or professional advice.','usage'),[Q(1,'Why is vitamin C included in the diet?','It supports normal tissue repair','It replaces all food','It is a type of protein tool','Sense 1 is a needed nutrient.','context'),Q(2,'What does she take each morning?','A supplement containing vitamins','A whole meal in capsule form','A doctor’s passport','Sense 2 uses vitamin for a pill or drop.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','vitamin D','vitamin of D','D vitaminly','English commonly places the letter after vitamin.','collocation'),Q(1,'The name vitamin was coined from vita, “life,” and…','amine','vocal','vogue','The historical name combined life with an early chemical classification.','word-formation')]);
P('vitascope','Vitascope is a coined name combining vita, “life,” with -scope, a viewing instrument; it named an early motion-picture projector.',C('vitascope.s1','film history','The museum’s vitascope projected moving photographic images onto a small screen.','博物馆的维太镜把活动摄影图像投射到小屏幕上。','early vitascope; project images with a vitascope','名词，指一种早期电影放映装置。','The device projects moving pictures.','早期放映机'),M('The vitascope projected only a single still photograph and could not show moving images.','The vitascope projected moving photographic images onto a screen.','The source sense identifies it as a moving-picture projector.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the museum’s vitascope project?','Moving photographic images','Only a printed map','A live radio broadcast','A vitascope was used to project moving pictures.','context'),Q(1,'A vitascope belongs to the history of…','motion-picture projection','passport inspection','electrical voltage measurement','It is an early projector.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','project images with a vitascope','vitascope images by measuring','a vitascope of moving to','The instrument projects images.','grammar'),Q(1,'The element -scope suggests…','an instrument for viewing','a person who sings','a quality of liveliness','The name combines life with a viewing instrument.','word-formation')]);
P('vitriolic','Vitriolic is formed from vitriol + -ic; vitriol was an old name for sulphuric acid, and the adjective also means bitterly hostile.',[C('vitriolic.s1','criticism','The columnist wrote a vitriolic review that attacked the actor personally instead of discussing the performance.','专栏作家写了一篇刻薄的评论，人身攻击演员而没有讨论演出。','vitriolic criticism/comment; a vitriolic attack','形容词，指充满强烈敌意，尤用于批评。','The review is bitter and personally hostile.','刻薄的'),C('vitriolic.s1','chemistry','Older laboratory texts describe vitriolic acid as a historical name for sulphuric acid.','旧版实验室教材把“矾油”列为硫酸的历史名称。','vitriolic acid; vitriol compounds','也可与vitriol有关，旧称硫酸。','The adjective refers to the acid’s historical name.','硫酸的')],M('Her vitriolic review praised the actor warmly and avoided every personal attack.','Her complimentary review praised the actor warmly and avoided every personal attack.','Warm praise is not hostile or vitriolic criticism.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why is the review called vitriolic?','It attacks the actor personally with hostility','It calmly lists ticket prices','It praises every part of the performance','The figurative sense is bitterly hostile criticism.','context'),Q(1,'What was “vitriolic acid” an older name for?','Sulphuric acid','Vitamin C','A salt-water solution','The historical chemical sense relates to vitriol.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which collocation is natural?','vitriolic criticism','vitriolic kindness','vitriolic applause for praise','The word commonly modifies criticism or attack.','collocation'),Q(1,'Vitriolic is derived from…','vitriol + -ic','vital + -ity','vocal + -ist','The adjective is based on the older term vitriol.','word-formation')]);
P('viva','Viva is short for viva voce, Latin for “by the living voice,” and means an oral examination.',C('viva.s1','education','She passed her viva after answering the examiners’ questions about her thesis.','她回答了考官关于论文的问题后，通过了口试。','doctoral viva; pass/take a viva','名词，尤指完成学位所需的口头考试。','The examiners question her orally about her work.','口试'),M('The student passed the viva without speaking or answering a single question.','The student passed the written examination without speaking or answering a question.','A viva is oral, so the student must speak and answer.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the examiners ask about?','Her thesis','Her passport visa','A theater projector','A viva tests the student orally on academic work.','context'),Q(1,'A viva is a form of…','oral examination','written driving permit','physical fitness test','The term names an oral exam.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','take a viva','take a viva voce paper exam silently','viva the thesis into','Students take or pass a viva.','collocation'),Q(1,'Viva is shortened from Latin…','viva voce, “by the living voice”','vis a vis, “face to face”','vita brevis, “short life”','The phrase explains the oral nature of the examination.','word-formation')]);
P('vivacity','Vivacity comes through French vivacité from Latin vivax, “lively,” and means cheerful energy or animation.',C('vivacity.s1','personality','Her vivacity kept the long train ride lively as she told stories and asked everyone questions.','她讲故事、问大家问题，让漫长的火车旅程一直充满活力。','natural vivacity; charm and vivacity','名词，指愉快的活力和生气勃勃。','Her animated manner enlivens the group.','活泼'),M('Her vivacity made the train ride lively because she sat silently and showed no interest.','Her quietness made the train ride subdued because she sat silently and showed no interest.','Silence and lack of interest show little vivacity.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did she show vivacity?','By telling stories and engaging everyone','By sitting silently without interest','By checking train voltage','Vivacity is cheerful energy and animation.','context'),Q(1,'A person with vivacity is likely…','lively and animated','dull and lifeless','unable to move','The noun names lively energy.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','charm and vivacity','vivacityly charm','a vivaciousness to','Vivacity is a noun that can pair with charm.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vivacity is historically related to…','Latin vivax, “lively”','Latin viscus, “organ”','French vis, “screw”','The source word describes liveliness.','word-formation')]);
P('vivid','Vivid comes from Latin vividus, from vivere, “live”; it describes a mental image that seems real or a very bright color.',[C('vivid.s1','memory','He gave a vivid account of the storm, describing the sound of the roof tiles as they flew away.','他生动地讲述了风暴，描述屋瓦被吹飞时的声音。','vivid memory/description; vividly remember','形容描写或记忆清晰得仿佛真实。','The details make the scene easy to imagine.','生动的'),C('vivid.s2','color','The artist used vivid orange and turquoise to make the poster stand out.','艺术家用鲜亮的橙色和绿松石色让海报醒目。','vivid color; vivid red/blue','形容颜色非常鲜艳明亮。','The strong colors catch attention.','鲜艳的')],M('The vivid orange poster was so pale that nobody could see its color.','The faded orange poster was so pale that nobody could see its color.','A vivid color is bright, not pale and hard to see.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What made his storm account vivid?','Specific sounds and details','A list of train fares','A blank page','Sense 1 means clear and lifelike in the mind.','context'),Q(2,'What colors made the poster vivid?','Orange and turquoise','Pale gray and beige only','Invisible ink','Sense 2 is bright, strong color.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a vivid memory','a vividness memory','memorize vivid','Vivid is an adjective modifying memory.','grammar'),Q(1,'A vivid description makes a scene…','seem clear and real in the mind','impossible to imagine','quiet in volume only','The word has a clarity/lifelike-image sense.','meaning')]);
P('vividly','Vividly is formed from vivid + -ly and means in bright color or with lifelike clarity.',C('vividly.s1','description','She vividly remembers the blue lanterns floating above the river on her first festival night.','她清楚地记得第一次参加节庆时，蓝灯笼漂浮在河面上的情景。','vividly remember/describe; vividly colored','副词，指色彩鲜明或记忆、描写极其清晰。','The memory is detailed and easy to picture.','清晰地'),M('He vividly described the scene, but his account was so vague that nobody could picture it.','He vaguely described the scene, and nobody could picture it.','A vivid description is clear enough to picture.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does she remember vividly?','Blue lanterns over the river','A voltage reading','A work visa','The adverb means she remembers it clearly.','context'),Q(1,'A vividly colored poster has…','bright, strong colors','colors too faint to notice','no color at all','The adverb can describe vivid colors.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which sentence is correct?','I vividly remember that night.','I vivid remember that night.','I remember vividness that night.','The -ly form modifies the verb remember.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vividly most nearly means…','clearly and in detail','reluctantly','without being noticed','It describes strong visual clarity.','meaning')]);
P('vividness','Vividness is vivid + -ness and names brilliance of color or lifelike clarity.',C('vividness.s1','art','The vividness of the mural comes from its saturated reds and sharp outlines.','壁画的鲜明感来自饱和的红色和清晰的轮廓。','vividness of color/memory; add vividness','名词，指颜色鲜明，或内容清晰得令人身临其境。','Strong pigments and outlines intensify the visual effect.','鲜明'),M('The vividness of the mural came from gray paint that made every outline disappear.','The dullness of the mural came from gray paint that made every outline disappear.','Gray paint and unclear outlines produce dullness, not vividness.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What creates the mural’s vividness?','Saturated reds and sharp outlines','Faded gray paint and blurred edges','A quiet room','The context ties vividness to strong color and clarity.','context'),Q(1,'Vividness can mean…','brightness of color or lifelike clarity','the quality of being silent','an ability to measure voltage','The noun names the quality of being vivid.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is natural?','the vividness of the image','the vividness to image','image vividnessly','The pattern is vividness of something.','grammar'),Q(1,'The suffix -ness turns vivid into…','a noun for a quality','a past-tense verb','a comparative adverb','Vividness names the state or quality of being vivid.','word-formation')]);
P('vivify','Vivify comes from Latin vivificare, “make alive,” from vivus “living” + facere “make”; it means make a scene or account livelier.',C('vivify.s1','writing','The added dialogue vivified the historical account and made the people seem real.','新增的对话让历史叙述生动起来，使人物仿佛真实存在。','vivify a scene/account; details vivify a story','动词，指使叙述、场景或人物更生动。','The dialogue brings the account to life.','使生动'),M('The extra dialogue vivified the account by removing every detail and making it lifeless.','The extra dialogue drained the account of life by removing every detail.','Vivify means make lively, not remove life and detail.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What vivified the historical account?','Added dialogue','A blank cover','A broken voltmeter','The dialogue made the account lively.','context'),Q(1,'To vivify a scene is to…','make it more lively','erase every character','measure its size','The verb means bring to life or animate.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which form is the past tense?','vivified','vivifyed','vivifing','Vivify changes final y to i before -ed.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vivify derives from Latin elements meaning…','living + make','see + speak','voice + measure','The historical formation means make alive.','word-formation')]);
P('viz','Viz is an abbreviation of Latin videlicet, “namely” or “that is to say,” used to introduce specific details.',C('viz.s1','writing','The team includes three experts, viz, a chemist, a botanist, and a geologist.','团队包括三位专家，即一名化学家、一名植物学家和一名地质学家。','viz. before a list; namely, viz.','缩写词，置于列举之前，表示后文给出具体内容。','The list specifies which three experts.','即'),M('The report wrote “viz” after the list to show that no details would follow.','The report wrote “viz” before the list to show that details would follow.','Viz introduces the specific details that follow.','usage'),[Q(1,'What does viz introduce?','The specific names of the three experts','A conclusion with no details','A person’s travel visa','Viz means namely or that is to say.','context'),Q(1,'Where does viz normally appear?','Before the details it introduces','Only at the very end of the list','Inside a passport number','It signals that specifics follow.','grammar'),Q(1,'Viz abbreviates…','videlicet','vitality','vocabulary','Its source is a Latin word meaning namely.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','three experts, viz, a chemist and two others','viz three experts are excluded','a visa viz to travel','Viz introduces a clarifying list.','usage')]);
P('vocabulary','Vocabulary comes through French from Latin vocabulum, “word/name,” from vocare, “call”; it means a person’s known words or a field’s word set.',[C('vocabulary.s1','learning','Reading widely helped Mina build a vocabulary she could use in academic discussions.','广泛阅读帮助米娜积累了能用于学术讨论的词汇。','build/expand vocabulary; active vocabulary','一个人认识并能使用的全部词语。','The words are available to her for speaking and writing.','个人词汇'),C('vocabulary.s2','language','The book explains the vocabulary of sailing, including terms for sails, ropes, and wind.','这本书解释了航海词汇，包括帆、绳索和风的术语。','technical vocabulary; vocabulary of a field','某种语言、书籍或领域使用的一组词。','The words belong to the subject of sailing.','领域词汇')],M('The book’s sailing vocabulary consisted only of terms used in cooking and medicine.','The book’s sailing vocabulary consisted of terms used for sails, ropes, and wind.','Cooking terms are not the word set used in sailing.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What helped Mina build her vocabulary?','Reading widely','Learning to measure voltage','Visiting a consulate','Sense 1 is the set of words one person knows.','context'),Q(2,'What does the book’s sailing vocabulary include?','Terms for sails, ropes, and wind','Only cooking words','A list of people’s passport numbers','Sense 2 is the word set of a subject field.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','expand your vocabulary','vocabulary of you expand','vocabularies your expand','Expand your vocabulary is a common collocation.','collocation'),Q(1,'Vocabulary ultimately relates to Latin vocare, “to…”','call','see','flow','The word family concerns naming or calling things.','word-formation')]);
P('vocal','Vocal comes from Latin vocalis, from vox, “voice”; it can mean related to singing, outspoken, or the sung part of music.',[C('vocal.s1','music','The singer warmed up her vocal cords before recording the song.','录歌前，歌手先活动了声带。','vocal range/cords; vocal performance','形容词，指与声音或歌唱有关。','The cords produce the singer’s voice.','声音的'),C('vocal.s2','opinion','Residents became vocal about the need for safer crossings after two accidents.','两起事故后，居民公开强烈表达了对安全人行横道的需求。','be vocal about something; vocal opposition','形容词，指大声、公开表达意见的。','The residents speak up about their concern.','直言的'),C('vocal.s3','recording','The recording places the vocal above a quiet piano accompaniment.','这段录音把人声置于轻柔的钢琴伴奏之上。','lead/backing vocals; vocal and instrumental parts','名词，指音乐作品中由人声演唱的部分。','The sung line is distinct from the instruments.','人声部分')],M('The residents were vocal about safer crossings because they refused to express any opinion.','The residents were silent about safer crossings because they refused to express any opinion.','Being vocal means expressing opinions openly, not withholding them.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the singer warm up?','Her vocal cords','The piano keys','The theater’s voltage','Sense 1 relates to voice and singing.','context'),Q(2,'How were residents vocal?','They spoke publicly about safer crossings','They kept every concern secret','They tuned a piano','Sense 2 is freely and strongly expressing an opinion.','context'),Q(3,'What did the recording place above the piano?','The sung vocal part','A passport stamp','A silent film','Sense 3 is the sung component of music.','context'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses vocal as an adjective?','vocal opposition to the plan','the lead vocal in the song','two vocals on the recording','The first phrase uses vocal to modify opposition.','grammar')]);
P('vocalist','Vocalist is formed from vocal + -ist and names a singer in a musical group, distinct from the instrumental players.',C('vocalist.s1','music','The band’s vocalist took the microphone while the guitarist checked the amplifier.','乐队的主唱拿起麦克风时，吉他手正在检查音箱。','lead vocalist; vocalist in a band','名词，指乐队中负责演唱的歌手。','The singer is distinguished from the instrumentalists.','主唱'),M('The band’s vocalist played the drums while another member sang every song.','The band’s drummer played the drums while another member sang every song.','A vocalist is the singer, not necessarily the drummer.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the vocalist take?','The microphone','The guitar amplifier','A voltage meter','The band’s singer takes the microphone.','context'),Q(1,'A vocalist is…','the singer in a musical group','the person who tunes every instrument','a person who sells concert tickets','The source sense specifically means a group’s singer.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','lead vocalist','vocalistly lead','a vocalist of instrumental','Vocalist is a person noun commonly modified by lead.','grammar'),Q(1,'The suffix -ist here forms…','a person who performs a role','a sound wave','an abstract quality','Vocalist names the singer.','word-formation')]);
P('vocalization','Vocalization comes from vocalize + -ation and names producing sounds with the voice or a consonant’s change into a vowel.',[C('vocalization.s1','speech','The baby’s vocalization changed from soft coos to loud repeated syllables.','婴儿发出的声音从轻柔咕哝变成了大声重复的音节。','vocalization of sounds; speech vocalization','指用嗓音发出声音的行为。','The child produces sounds with the voice.','发声'),C('vocalization.s2','phonology','The linguist described the vocalization of a consonant in the historical pronunciation.','语言学家描述了历史发音中一个辅音向元音的转变。','vocalization of a consonant; sound change','语音学中指辅音音素转变为元音。','A consonant becomes vowel-like in the sound history.','元音化')],M('The linguist called it vocalization because a vowel changed into a consonant.','The linguist called it consonantization because a vowel changed into a consonant.','Vocalization is the change toward a vowel, not away from one.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened to the baby’s vocalization?','It developed into repeated syllables','It became a written visa','It stopped involving the voice','Sense 1 concerns sounds produced by the voice.','context'),Q(2,'What changed in the linguist’s example?','A consonant became vowel-like','A vowel became a visa','A word became a picture','Sense 2 is a sound change toward a vowel.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','vocalization of a consonant','vocalization a consonant into','vocalizationly consonant','The noun takes of to identify the sound being changed.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vocalization can describe…','voice-sound production or a consonant becoming a vowel','a device that projects films','the right to vote','The entry includes both vocal and phonological senses.','meaning')]);
P('vocalize','Vocalize is vocal + -ize and means utter sounds, sing without words, or express a thought aloud.',C('vocalize.s1','speech','The baby began to vocalize when the familiar song played, making soft sounds between the notes.','熟悉的歌曲响起时，婴儿开始发声，在音符间发出轻柔的声音。','vocalize a thought; vocalize sounds','动词，指发出声音、无词歌唱或把想法说出来。','The baby produces vocal sounds.','发声'),M('The infant vocalized by staying completely silent throughout the song.','The infant vocalized by making soft sounds during the song.','Vocalize means utter a sound, not remain silent.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the baby do when the song played?','Made soft vocal sounds','Wrote down the melody','Measured the speaker’s voltage','Vocalize means produce sounds with the voice.','context'),Q(1,'A singer may vocalize without words by…','singing sounds or notes','writing a review','tuning a guitar silently','The verb can mean sing without lyrics.','meaning'),Q(1,'Choose the correct form: She ___ her concern aloud.','vocalized','vocalization','vocalizingly','The sentence needs a past-tense verb.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vocalize is formed from…','vocal + -ize','vogue + -ist','visit + -or','The suffix -ize forms the verb meaning give voice to.','word-formation')]);
P('vocation','Vocation comes from Latin vocatio, “a calling,” from vocare, “call”; it means a fitting profession or a strong sense of duty toward work.',[C('vocation.s1','career','After trying several jobs, she found a vocation in wildlife conservation that suited her skills.','尝试几份工作后，她在野生动物保护领域找到了适合自己技能的职业。','find/choose a vocation; vocational calling','适合个人能力与兴趣的职业。','The work fits her abilities and interests.','职业'),C('vocation.s2','calling','He felt a vocation to teach children in remote communities, not just a desire for a salary.','他感到自己有志于去偏远社区教孩子，这不只是为了薪水。','feel/have a vocation; a vocation to serve','强烈感到某项工作是自己应当从事的使命。','He feels called to this work.','使命感')],M('She found her vocation in conservation, a job that had no connection to her interests or abilities.','She found her vocation in conservation, a job that matched her interests and abilities.','A vocation is work suited to the person or felt as a calling.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What suited her skills?','A job in wildlife conservation','A machine for projecting film','A trip across the ocean','Sense 1 is a fitting profession.','context'),Q(2,'Why did he want to teach remotely?','He felt called to serve children','He wanted only a larger salary','He was assigned to repair a vise','Sense 2 is a strong inner calling.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is idiomatic?','a vocation to teach','a vocation of teaching to','vocationly teach','The pattern a vocation to do something is natural.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vocation is historically related to Latin vocare, “to…”','call','see','flow','A vocation was figuratively a calling to work.','word-formation')]);
P('vocational','Vocational is formed from vocation + -al and means related to job-specific skills, education, or training.',C('vocational.s1','education','The college offers vocational courses in plumbing, nursing, and electrical repair.','这所学院开设管道维修、护理和电气维修等职业课程。','vocational education/training; vocational skills','形容词，指与特定职业所需技能和培训有关。','The courses prepare students for particular jobs.','职业的'),M('Vocational training prepared her for a trade by avoiding every practical skill.','Vocational training prepared her for a trade by teaching practical job skills.','Job training develops practical skills rather than avoiding them.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does the college’s vocational training teach?','Skills for specific jobs','The history of ocean voyages only','How to write a passport','Vocational courses prepare learners for occupations.','context'),Q(1,'A vocational course is…','job-related and skills-focused','a course with no practical use','a type of vacation','The adjective relates to work training.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','vocational training','vocationally training as adjective','training vocationly','Vocational is the adjective modifying training.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vocational is formed from…','vocation + -al','vocal + -ist','vogue + -ly','The suffix -al makes an adjective from vocation.','word-formation')]);
P('vogue','Vogue came through French vogue, “fashion or style,” and means a popular style or widespread popularity for a time.',[C('vogue.s1','fashion','Long coats came back into vogue after several designers featured them in autumn shows.','几位设计师在秋季时装秀上展示长外套后，这种款式又流行起来。','come into/go out of vogue; in vogue','名词，指一段时间内很多人追随的风格或习俗。','The style becomes fashionable again.','时尚'),C('vogue.s2','popularity','For a while, home fermentation was in vogue among city cooks and food writers.','有一段时间，家庭发酵在城市厨师和美食作家中很流行。','in vogue; popularity of an idea','指某种观念或活动广受欢迎。','Many people adopt the activity temporarily.','流行')],M('The style came into vogue when hardly anyone followed it and every designer rejected it.','The style fell out of vogue when hardly anyone followed it and every designer rejected it.','A style followed by almost nobody is not in vogue.','meaning'),[Q(1,'When did long coats come back into vogue?','After designers featured them in autumn shows','Before clothing existed','After every designer rejected them','Sense 1 is a style becoming fashionable.','context'),Q(2,'What became popular among city cooks?','Home fermentation','A new voltage standard','Visa applications','Sense 2 concerns widespread popularity of an activity.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is idiomatic?','come into vogue','come in a vogue to','vogue into came','The phrase come into vogue means become fashionable.','collocation'),Q(1,'Vogue is closest to…','fashion or temporary popularity','an official document','a painful illness','The French source word means fashion or style.','meaning')]);
P('voice','Voice comes through Old French from Latin vox, vocem, “voice or speech,” related to vocare, “call”; it covers sound, expression, grammar, and expressing thoughts.',[C('voice.s1','speech','Her voice grew hoarse after she spoke for three hours at the conference.','她在会议上连续讲了三个小时后，嗓音变得沙哑。','speaking/singing voice; raise one’s voice','名词，指人说话或唱歌发出的声音。','The vocal organs produce the sound.','嗓音'),C('voice.s2','rights','The residents finally had a voice in the decision about the new road.','居民终于能参与新道路的决策并表达意见。','have/give someone a voice; a voice in something','指表达意见的权利或能力。','Residents can now express their views.','发言权'),C('voice.s3','grammar','In “The ball was kicked,” the verb is in the passive voice.','在“The ball was kicked”中，动词使用被动语态。','active/passive voice; change voice','指动词形式，表示主语执行动作还是承受动作。','The subject receives the action.','语态'),C('voice.s4','expression','She voiced her concern that the bridge was not safe for heavy trucks.','她表达了对桥梁无法安全承载重型卡车的担忧。','voice an opinion/concern; voice support','动词，指说出自己的想法或感受。','She states the concern aloud.','表达')],M('The residents had a voice in the decision, meaning they were forbidden to express any opinion.','The residents had no voice in the decision, meaning they were forbidden to express an opinion.','Having a voice means having the ability or right to express a view.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did her voice grow hoarse?','She spoke for three hours','She visited the bridge','She changed the sentence to passive','Sense 1 is the sound from the vocal organs.','context'),Q(2,'What did residents gain?','A chance to express their views','A new vocal cord','A grammar rule','Sense 2 is the right to participate or be heard.','context'),Q(3,'In the ball sentence, what does voice refer to?','The verb’s active or passive form','The sound volume','A resident’s opinion','Sense 3 is the grammatical category.','meaning'),Q(4,'To voice a concern is to…','express it aloud or clearly','hide it from everyone','sing without words','Sense 4 uses voice as a verb meaning express.','meaning')]);
P('void','Void comes through Old French from Latin vocitus/void of content in form history; it can mean an empty space, legally invalid, empty of something, or officially cancel.',[C('void.s1','space','After the warehouse was emptied, a vast void remained where the storage tanks had stood.','仓库清空后，储罐原来所在的位置留下了一大片空处。','a void in space; fill a void','名词，指大块空处，也可指失落感。','The tanks are gone, leaving empty space.','空处'),C('void.s2','law','The court ruled that the contract was void because one signature had been forged.','法院裁定合同无效，因为其中一个签名是伪造的。','declare a contract void; legally void','形容词，指没有法律效力。','A forged signature invalidates the agreement.','无效的'),C('void.s3','absence','The report was void of evidence linking the suspect to the scene.','报告中没有任何证据能把嫌疑人与现场联系起来。','void of something; completely void of','形容词，指缺少某物、没有某物。','No connecting evidence is present.','缺乏'),C('void.s4','administration','The agency voided the duplicate permit and issued one corrected document.','机构注销了重复许可证，并签发了一份更正后的文件。','void a permit/transaction; void a result','动词，指正式宣布结果或文件无效。','The duplicate permit is cancelled officially.','使无效')],M('The court found the contract void, so it remained fully enforceable in law.','The court found the contract valid, so it remained enforceable in law.','A void contract has no legal force.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What remained after the tanks were removed?','A large empty space','A signed contract','A stack of permits','Sense 1 is a physical empty area.','context'),Q(2,'Why was the contract void?','A signature had been forged','It contained too much evidence','The parties fulfilled every term','Sense 2 means legally invalid.','context'),Q(3,'A report void of evidence…','contains no relevant evidence','contains strong proof','is a permit form','Sense 3 means empty of something.','meaning'),Q(4,'What did the agency do to the duplicate permit?','Officially cancelled it','Made it legally stronger','Filed it as evidence','Sense 4 is the verb meaning annul.','context')]);
P('volatile','Volatile comes from Latin volatilis, “able to fly,” from volare, “fly”; it describes sudden change, easy evaporation, or an unstable mood/situation.',[C('volatile.s1','markets','The volatile share price rose and fell sharply after each announcement.','每次公告发布后，这只股票的价格都剧烈波动。','volatile market/prices; remain volatile','指可能突然且不可预测地变化。','The price shifts rapidly in both directions.','波动的'),C('volatile.s2','chemistry','The solvent is volatile, so it evaporates quickly when left in an open dish.','这种溶剂具有挥发性，敞口放置时会迅速蒸发。','volatile liquid/compound; volatile substance','指容易从液体变成气体的。','The liquid quickly enters the air.','易挥发的'),C('volatile.s3','temperament','The volatile manager could become angry without warning during routine meetings.','这位情绪不稳定的经理会在例行会议中毫无预兆地发怒。','volatile mood/temper; politically volatile','指情绪易变或局势可能突然变得危险。','His mood shifts quickly and unpredictably.','情绪不稳的')],M('The volatile price stayed exactly the same for years and never changed.','The stable price stayed exactly the same for years and never changed.','A volatile price changes suddenly; a fixed price is stable.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the share price behave?','It rose and fell sharply','It stayed unchanged for years','It was converted into a solvent','Sense 1 is sudden unpredictable change.','context'),Q(2,'Why is the solvent volatile?','It evaporates quickly','It freezes at room temperature','It cannot become a gas','Sense 2 concerns ease of evaporation.','context'),Q(3,'What was the manager’s temperament?','Quick to change and become angry','Always calm and predictable','Unable to speak','Sense 3 concerns unstable mood.','meaning'),Q(1,'Volatile derives from Latin volare, meaning…','to fly','to call','to see','The etymological image is something that can fly away.','word-formation')]);
P('volatility','Volatility is volatile + -ity and names sudden unpredictability or a liquid’s tendency to evaporate.',[C('volatility.s1','finance','Investors expected high volatility because the company’s earnings changed sharply each quarter.','由于公司每季度收益变化剧烈，投资者预期市场波动性很高。','price/market volatility; measure volatility','名词，指突然、难以预测地变化的倾向。','The figures fluctuate sharply.','波动性'),C('volatility.s2','chemistry','The solvent’s volatility makes it evaporate rapidly in a warm laboratory.','这种溶剂的挥发性使它在温暖的实验室里迅速蒸发。','volatility of a liquid; high volatility','名词，指液体迅速转化为气体的性质。','The liquid readily enters the air.','挥发性')],M('The solvent’s volatility kept it liquid in an open dish for several weeks.','The solvent’s low volatility kept it liquid in an open dish for several weeks.','High volatility means a liquid evaporates readily.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did investors expect market volatility?','Earnings changed sharply each quarter','Earnings never changed','The solvent was stored nearby','Sense 1 is unpredictable fluctuation.','context'),Q(2,'What does solvent volatility cause?','Rapid evaporation','Permanent freezing','A higher voice','Sense 2 is the tendency to become vapor.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is common?','price volatility','volatility pricefully','prices volatilely noun','Volatility is a noun commonly following price.','grammar'),Q(1,'Volatility is the noun form of…','volatile','volitionally','volunteer','The suffix -ity names the quality or tendency.','word-formation')]);
P('volcanic','Volcanic is volcano + -ic and means related to a volcano or suddenly violent like an eruption.',[C('volcanic.s1','geology','Volcanic ash covered the village after the nearby mountain erupted.','附近火山喷发后，火山灰覆盖了村庄。','volcanic ash/rock/activity; volcanic island','形容词，指与火山有关或由火山造成。','The ash came from an eruption.','火山的'),C('volcanic.s2','emotion','A volcanic argument erupted when both negotiators accused each other of breaking the agreement.','双方谈判代表互相指责对方违约，争论骤然变得激烈。','volcanic anger/temper; volcanic argument','比喻突然猛烈、如火山爆发般的。','The argument becomes explosively violent.','猛烈的')],M('Volcanic ash came from a quiet lake with no volcano or eruption nearby.','Lake sediment came from a quiet lake with no volcano or eruption nearby.','Volcanic ash is produced by volcanic activity, not a quiet lake.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What covered the village?','Ash from the nearby eruption','Snow from a blizzard','A layer of fresh paint','Sense 1 relates to a volcano.','context'),Q(2,'Why was the argument volcanic?','It became suddenly intense and explosive','It was quiet and carefully scheduled','It took place underwater','Sense 2 is a metaphor for explosive intensity.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which collocation is natural?','volcanic ash','volcanic politeness','ash volcanoically','Volcanic commonly modifies ash or rock.','collocation'),Q(1,'Volcanic is formed from…','volcano + -ic','voltage + -meter','vocal + -ist','The suffix -ic makes an adjective from volcano.','word-formation')]);
P('volcanism','Volcanism is volcano + -ism and names the processes by which magma reaches Earth’s surface.',C('volcanism.s1','geology','The field team studied volcanism by mapping lava flows and measuring gases around the crater.','野外团队通过绘制熔岩流分布并测量火山口周边气体来研究火山活动。','study volcanism; volcanic processes','名词，指岩浆到达地表的一系列地质过程。','The scientists investigate magma and eruption processes.','火山活动'),M('The study of volcanism examined glaciers and ice sheets while excluding magma and eruptions.','The study of glaciology examined glaciers and ice sheets while excluding magma and eruptions.','Volcanism concerns magma reaching the surface, not glaciers.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the field team map?','Lava flows','A city’s bus routes','A volleyball court','Volcanism research studies volcanic processes.','context'),Q(1,'Volcanism concerns…','processes by which magma reaches the surface','the measurement of sound volume','a mouse species','That is the geological definition.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','study volcanism','volcanismly study','volcanize the study of','Volcanism is a noun naming a process or field.','grammar'),Q(1,'The suffix -ism can form a noun for…','a process or system','a person who measures voltage','a color only','Here volcanism names geological processes.','word-formation')]);
P('volcano','Volcano came from Italian vulcano, “burning mountain,” from Latin Vulcanus, the Roman fire god; it names an erupting mountain or a situation ready to erupt.',[C('volcano.s1','geology','The volcano sent ash and gas high into the air before lava flowed down its slope.','火山先把火山灰和气体喷向高空，随后熔岩沿山坡流下。','active/dormant volcano; volcanic eruption','名词，指可喷出熔岩、火山灰和气体的山体。','The mountain erupts material from its crater.','火山'),C('volcano.s2','figurative','With both teams still angry, the meeting room felt like a volcano ready to erupt.','双方队伍仍怒气未消，会议室仿佛一座即将喷发的火山。','a political/social volcano; ready to erupt','比喻随时可能突然变得暴力或混乱的局面。','Tension may explode into conflict.','一触即发')],M('The volcano erupted, but it was a river valley with no crater or molten rock.','The volcano erupted, sending ash and molten rock from its crater.','An erupting mountain with a crater and molten rock is a volcano.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What came from the volcano first?','Ash and gas','Snow and wheat','A printed voucher','Sense 1 is an erupting mountain.','context'),Q(2,'Why did the meeting room feel like a volcano?','Anger could suddenly erupt into conflict','The room was filled with lava','Everyone had left peacefully','Sense 2 describes a tense situation likely to explode.','context'),Q(1,'The word volcano came through Italian…','vulcano, “burning mountain”','vocale, “sung part”','visita, “visit”','The word is linked to Italian and the Roman fire god.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','an active volcano','a volcanos mountain','an erupt volcano','Volcano is a count noun and active is its adjective.','grammar')]);
P('vole','Vole is short for vole-mouse, literally “field-mouse,” with its first element probably related to Old Norse völlr, “field.”',C('vole.s1','wildlife','A vole darted through the grass and disappeared into a shallow burrow.','一只田鼠穿过草丛，钻进浅洞里消失了。','field vole; vole burrow; small vole','名词，指生活在草地或洞穴中的短尾小型啮齿动物。','The small rodent moves through grass and burrows.','田鼠'),M('The vole was a large whale that surfaced beside the boat.','The vole was a small rodent that burrowed in the grass.','A vole is a small rodent, not a whale.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where did the vole disappear?','Into a shallow burrow','Into a passport','Across a volleyball net','The context shows a small burrowing rodent.','context'),Q(1,'A vole is most likely to live…','in grassland or a burrow','in the open sea','inside a volcano crater','The source describes a small rodent in grassland or burrows.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a field vole','a vole of fielding','a vole sea mammal','Vole-mouse historically means field mouse.','collocation'),Q(1,'Vole is short for…','vole-mouse','voltmeter','vocalist','The word was shortened from vole-mouse.','word-formation')]);
P('volleyball','Volleyball was named in 1896 from volley + ball because players return the ball before it hits the ground.',[C('volleyball.s1','sport','Our volleyball team won the final by keeping the ball in play over the net.','我们的排球队把球持续击过球网，赢得了决赛。','play volleyball; volleyball team/court','名词，指球员用手将球击过球网、不让球落地的团队运动。','The teams return the ball before it touches the ground.','排球运动'),C('volleyball.s2','equipment','She packed a volleyball in the car so the group could play at the beach.','她把一个排球放进车里，大家可以在海滩上玩。','a volleyball; inflate the volleyball','名词，指这项运动所用的球。','The object is the ball used in the game.','排球')],M('They played volleyball by letting the ball touch the ground after every serve.','They played volleyball by returning the ball over the net before it touched the ground.','The sport requires returning the ball before it hits the ground.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the team win?','By keeping the ball in play over the net','By carrying it across the court','By letting it rest on the ground','Sense 1 is the game.','context'),Q(2,'What did she pack?','The ball used for the game','A net with no ball','A voltage meter','Sense 2 names the equipment.','context'),Q(1,'The name volleyball combines volley + ball because…','players return the ball while it is in flight','players roll the ball on the ground','the game uses no ball','The name refers to striking the ball before it lands.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses volleyball as a noun for the sport?','We play volleyball after school.','She inflated a volleyball.','The volleyball was blue.','The first sentence names the game; the others refer to the ball.','grammar')]);
P('volt','Volt is named after Italian physicist Alessandro Volta and is the SI unit of electric potential difference.',[C('volt.s1','physics','The battery supplies twelve volts to the small motor.','电池向小型电机提供十二伏特电压。','one volt; measure in volts','名词，指电势差和电动势的国际单位。','The number states electric potential difference.','伏特'),C('volt.s2','equipment','This device needs a supply of at least five volts to operate reliably.','这台设备需要至少五伏特的电源才能稳定运行。','five/twelve volts; voltage rating in volts','也指某设备或电源中规定的伏特数值。','The rating specifies the amount for the device.','伏特数值')],M('The motor requires twelve volts, but the battery supplies no electrical potential at all.','The motor requires twelve volts, and the battery supplies that electric potential.','A requirement of twelve volts is not met by zero electrical potential.','measurement'),[Q(1,'What does the battery supply?','Twelve volts to the motor','Twelve liters of water','A five-meter cable','A volt measures electrical potential difference.','context'),Q(2,'What does the device’s five-volt rating state?','The required amount of electrical potential','Its weight','The volume of its case','Sense 2 is a stated amount of volts.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which unit is abbreviated V?','volt','voltmeter','voltage','Volt is the unit symbolized by V.','measurement'),Q(1,'The unit is named after…','Alessandro Volta','a volcano','a volleyball inventor','The volt honors the Italian physicist.','word-formation')]);
P('voltage','Voltage is formed from volt + -age and means electrical potential difference or the particular amount supplied to equipment.',[C('voltage.s1','circuits','The voltage pushes electric current through the circuit and is measured in volts.','电压推动电流通过电路，单位是伏特。','electric voltage; voltage across a circuit','指推动电流流动、以伏特测量的电势差。','The electrical potential drives current.','电压'),C('voltage.s2','equipment','Check the label to confirm that the appliance’s voltage matches the wall supply.','查看标签，确认电器电压与墙上电源相匹配。','supply/mains voltage; operating voltage','指机器或电路某部分使用的具体电压值。','The appliance must match the supply amount.','电压值')],M('The appliance’s voltage must match the wall supply, so ignore the label and connect any source.','The appliance’s voltage must match the wall supply, so check the label before connecting it.','Mismatched voltage can damage equipment; matching is essential.','context'),[Q(1,'What pushes current through the circuit?','Voltage','A river current','A museum visitor','Sense 1 is electrical potential difference.','context'),Q(2,'What should the label confirm?','That appliance voltage matches the supply','That the appliance is a volleyball','That the plug is a visa','Sense 2 is the particular operating amount.','context'),Q(1,'Voltage is measured in…','volts','liters','meters per second','The volt is the unit of voltage.','measurement'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','supply voltage','voltageful supply','voltsage supply','Voltage commonly modifies supply or circuit.','collocation')]);
P('voltmeter','Voltmeter combines volt + meter and names an instrument for measuring voltage.',C('voltmeter.s1','electronics','Use a voltmeter across the battery terminals to check whether the supply is nine volts.','把电压表接在电池两端，检查电源是否为九伏特。','digital voltmeter; measure voltage with a voltmeter','名词，用于测量电压的仪表。','The device reads potential difference.','电压表'),M('She used a voltmeter to measure the battery’s mass in kilograms.','She used a balance to measure the battery’s mass in kilograms.','A voltmeter measures voltage, not mass.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where should the voltmeter be connected?','Across the battery terminals','Around the player’s neck','Inside a book cover','It measures the potential difference between terminals.','context'),Q(1,'What does a voltmeter measure?','Voltage','Temperature','The amount of water','The instrument is designed to read voltage.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','read the voltage with a voltmeter','read the voltage with a volleyball','voltmeter the battery’s weight','A voltmeter reads voltage.','collocation'),Q(1,'The compound voltmeter joins…','volt + meter','vocal + meter','vogue + measure','The name states what the meter measures.','word-formation')]);
P('volume','Volume comes from Latin volumen, “a roll or scroll,” from volvere, “roll”; it can mean space occupied, loudness, a book in a series, or a large amount of business.',[C('volume.s1','measurement','The box’s volume is two cubic meters, although it weighs very little.','这个箱子的体积是两立方米，尽管它很轻。','calculate/measure volume; volume of a box','名词，指物体或物质占据的空间量。','Cubic meters measure the space it fills.','体积'),C('volume.s2','sound','Please lower the volume because the baby is sleeping in the next room.','请把音量调低，隔壁房间的婴儿正在睡觉。','turn up/down the volume; volume level','名词，指声音有多响。','Lowering it makes the sound quieter.','音量'),C('volume.s3','publishing','Volume two of the atlas contains maps of the northern region.','这本地图集的第二卷收录了北部地区的地图。','the first/second volume; volume of a series','名词，指系列中的一本书。','It is one book in a multi-part work.','卷册'),C('volume.s4','business','The store handled a high volume of orders during the holiday season.','假日期间，这家商店处理了大量订单。','high/large volume of sales/orders; business volume','指业务或交易的总量、数量很大。','Many orders were processed.','大量')],M('The radio’s volume was too high, so I turned it up further to make it quieter.','The radio’s volume was too high, so I turned it down to make it quieter.','Turning volume up makes sound louder; turning it down makes it quieter.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does two cubic meters describe?','The box’s volume','Its weight','Its color','Sense 1 measures space occupied.','context'),Q(2,'Why lower the volume?','The baby is sleeping nearby','The box is too heavy','The atlas has two books','Sense 2 is sound loudness.','context'),Q(3,'What is volume two?','A book in the atlas series','The atlas’s physical size only','The radio sound level','Sense 3 means one book in a series.','context'),Q(4,'What did the store handle in high volume?','Orders','Cubic meters','Songs','Sense 4 concerns a large amount of business.','context')]);
P('voluminous','Voluminous comes from volume + -ous and describes a very large or extensive book/record, or loose full clothing.',[C('voluminous.s1','records','The lawyers reviewed a voluminous archive containing thousands of pages.','律师们查阅了一份篇幅浩大的档案，里面有数千页。','voluminous records/correspondence; voluminous book','指书籍或记录篇幅很长、内容量很大。','The archive contains a very large quantity of material.','浩繁的'),C('voluminous.s2','clothing','She wore a voluminous coat with wide sleeves that billowed in the wind.','她穿着一件宽袖蓬松的大衣，袖子在风中鼓起。','voluminous skirt/sleeves; loose and voluminous','指衣服宽大、松垂而蓬松。','The coat has abundant loose fabric.','宽松蓬松的')],M('The voluminous archive contained one brief note and nothing else.','The slim archive contained one brief note and nothing else.','A one-note archive is not extensive or voluminous.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why was the archive voluminous?','It contained thousands of pages','It held a single note','It was a narrow sleeve','Sense 1 describes extensive records.','context'),Q(2,'What made the coat voluminous?','Its wide sleeves and abundant fabric','Its tight fit and thin material','Its small pocket','Sense 2 describes loose, full clothing.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','voluminous correspondence','voluminously records','a volumeous archive','Voluminous is the adjective modifying correspondence.','grammar'),Q(1,'Voluminous is related to…','volume, an amount or size','voltage, electric force','vowel, a speech sound','The adjective describes a large volume or fullness.','word-formation')]);
P('voluntarily','Voluntarily is voluntary + -ly and means willingly, without force or compulsion.',C('voluntarily.s1','choice','She voluntarily joined the neighborhood cleanup, even though nobody had asked her to help.','尽管没人要求她帮忙，她还是自愿加入了社区清洁活动。','act/participate voluntarily; volunteer voluntarily','副词，指自愿地、并非受强迫地。','She chooses to take part.','自愿地'),M('He voluntarily signed the form because guards threatened to punish him if he refused.','He signed the form under pressure because guards threatened to punish him.','A threat is coercion, so the action was not voluntary.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did she join the cleanup?','She chose to help without being asked','She was ordered by a judge','She was paid by the neighborhood','Voluntarily means by one’s own choice.','context'),Q(1,'If a person acts voluntarily, they act…','willingly and without compulsion','only because of a threat','without knowing what they are doing','The adverb contrasts choice with force.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which sentence is natural?','She voluntarily offered to help.','She voluntary offered to help.','She volunteeredly to help.','The adverb modifies the verb offered.','grammar'),Q(1,'Voluntarily is formed from…','voluntary + -ly','volunteer + -hood','volume + -ly','The suffix forms an adverb from voluntary.','word-formation')]);
P('voluntary','Voluntary comes from Latin voluntarius, from voluntas, “will”; it means willingly done, unpaid service, or deliberate rather than accidental action.',[C('voluntary.s1','choice','The agreement was voluntary, and both sides could refuse without penalty.','这项协议是自愿的，双方都可以拒绝而不受处罚。','voluntary agreement/action; on a voluntary basis','指自愿进行、未受强迫。','Neither side is compelled to agree.','自愿的'),C('voluntary.s2','service','She does voluntary work at the food bank every Saturday without receiving pay.','她每周六都在食品银行做志愿工作，不领取报酬。','voluntary work/service; voluntary organization','指无偿帮助他人的工作。','She helps without being paid.','志愿的'),C('voluntary.s3','deliberate action','The damage was voluntary, not an accident: he knowingly cut the safety cable.','损坏是故意的，不是意外：他明知故犯地剪断了安全缆绳。','voluntary act; voluntary movement','指有意而为、并非意外发生的。','The action was intentional.','故意的')],M('The voluntary agreement was forced on both sides under threat of punishment.','The coerced agreement was forced on both sides under threat of punishment.','An agreement imposed by threats is not voluntary.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Could either side refuse the agreement?','Yes, without penalty','No, punishment was guaranteed','Only after signing','Sense 1 means not forced.','context'),Q(2,'Why was her work voluntary?','She was unpaid while helping at the food bank','She received a large salary','She was forced to work','Sense 2 is unpaid service.','context'),Q(3,'Why was cutting the cable voluntary?','He knowingly did it on purpose','The cable broke by accident','A storm caused it','Sense 3 means deliberate, not accidental.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','voluntary service','voluntarily service','service voluntarilyly','Voluntary is an adjective modifying service.','grammar')]);
P('volunteer','Volunteer comes through French volontaire from Latin voluntarius, “willing”; it can name an unpaid helper or a person who offers or says something unasked.',[C('volunteer.s1','service','A volunteer at the shelter served dinner and helped visitors find warm clothing.','收容所的一名志愿者分发晚餐，并帮来访者找到保暖衣物。','volunteer worker; recruit volunteers','名词，指无偿工作的人，也可指自愿参军者。','The helper serves without pay.','志愿者'),C('volunteer.s2','offer','No one asked, but Ravi volunteered to organize the book sale.','没人提出要求，但拉维主动提出组织图书义卖。','volunteer to do something; volunteer for a task','动词，指主动提出无偿做某事。','He offers before being asked.','主动提出'),C('volunteer.s3','information','She volunteered that she had seen the missing key on the desk.','她主动说自己看见丢失的钥匙在桌上。','volunteer information/a fact; volunteer that…','动词，指未经询问就主动告诉别人某事。','She supplies information without prompting.','主动透露')],M('Ravi volunteered to organize the sale after refusing to help and telling no one he could do it.','Ravi declined to organize the sale after refusing to help and telling no one he could do it.','Someone who volunteers offers help; refusing is the opposite.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the shelter volunteer do?','Served dinner and helped visitors','Sold military equipment','Measured the building’s voltage','Sense 1 is an unpaid helper.','context'),Q(2,'What did Ravi offer to do?','Organize the book sale','Hide the books','Ask someone else to volunteer','Sense 2 is offering to do a task.','context'),Q(3,'What did she volunteer?','That she had seen the key','A request for a passport visa','A list of vowels','Sense 3 means give information without being asked.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','volunteer to organize','volunteer for organize','volunteer organizing to','Volunteer is followed by to + verb when offering an action.','grammar')]);
P('vomit','Vomit comes from Latin vomere, “to eject,” and functions as both a verb for bringing stomach contents up and a noun for that material.',[C('vomit.s1','health','The patient began to vomit after the infection upset his stomach.','感染导致胃部不适后，病人开始呕吐。','vomit food/liquid; begin to vomit','动词，指把胃里的食物或液体经口吐出。','The contents come up from the stomach.','呕吐'),C('vomit.s2','health','The nurse cleaned the vomit from the floor and replaced the patient’s blanket.','护士清理了地板上的呕吐物，并给病人换了毯子。','clean up vomit; vomit on the floor','名词，指从胃里吐出的食物或液体。','Here the word names the material.','呕吐物')],M('The patient vomited by keeping all food in the stomach and swallowing it normally.','The patient kept the food down instead of vomiting.','Vomiting expels stomach contents rather than keeping them down.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the patient begin to do?','Bring stomach contents up','Measure his vital signs','Take a sea voyage','Sense 1 is the action of vomiting.','context'),Q(2,'What did the nurse clean from the floor?','The vomit','A voltage reading','A passport photograph','Sense 2 is the material brought up.','context'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses vomit as a noun?','The nurse cleaned the vomit.','The patient may vomit.','She vomited after lunch.','The first sentence has the as a noun marker.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vomit comes from Latin vomere, meaning…','to eject or throw up','to see clearly','to call someone','Its source verb describes expelling stomach contents.','word-formation')]);
P('voracious','Voracious comes from Latin vorax, “devouring,” from vorare, “to swallow”; it describes a huge appetite or extreme eagerness.',C('voracious.s1','reading','A voracious reader, Kim finishes two novels each week and always asks for another recommendation.','金是个如饥似渴的读者，每周读完两本小说，总会再要一本推荐。','voracious appetite/reader; voracious for knowledge','形容食欲极大，也比喻对书籍、工作或信息极其渴求。','The reader consumes books eagerly.','如饥似渴的'),M('The voracious reader never opened a book and avoided reading whenever possible.','The reluctant reader never opened a book and avoided reading whenever possible.','A voracious reader eagerly consumes books.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How often does Kim finish novels?','Two each week','One every ten years','None at all','The frequency shows a voracious appetite for reading.','context'),Q(1,'A voracious appetite is…','extremely large','completely absent','limited to one bite','Voracious means having a huge appetite.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a voracious reader','a reader voraciousness','voraciously reader','Voracious is an adjective before reader.','grammar'),Q(1,'The figurative use of voracious can describe…','great eagerness for information','a metal measuring tool','a quiet dislike of books','The word extends from eating to consuming knowledge or work.','meaning')]);
P('voracity','Voracity is formed from voracious + -ity and means an extreme appetite for food or intense eagerness for something.',[C('voracity.s1','food','The voracity of the hungry hikers surprised the cook, who had prepared only one pot of stew.','饥饿的徒步者食欲之大让厨师吃惊，他只准备了一锅炖菜。','voracity for food; satisfy someone’s voracity','名词，指极大的食欲。','They eat the food quickly and in large quantities.','食欲'),C('voracity.s2','ambition','The researcher’s voracity for knowledge led her to study three languages at once.','这位研究者对知识的强烈渴求促使她同时学习三种语言。','voracity for knowledge/power; intellectual voracity','比喻对知识、金钱或其他事物极其渴求。','She eagerly pursues more knowledge.','渴求')],M('The hikers’ voracity for food was shown by their refusing to eat a single bite.','The hikers’ lack of appetite was shown by their refusing to eat a single bite.','Refusing food shows little appetite, not voracity.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What surprised the cook?','How much the hikers wanted to eat','Their refusal to eat','Their knowledge of languages','Sense 1 is extreme appetite.','context'),Q(2,'What did the researcher seek eagerly?','Knowledge','A bowl of stew only','A new volleyball','Sense 2 is figurative eagerness.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','voracity for knowledge','knowledge voracityly','voracity to knowledge of','Voracity is followed by for to name the object of eagerness.','grammar'),Q(1,'Voracity is the noun form of…','voracious','vortex','voluntary','The -ity suffix makes a noun for the quality.','word-formation')]);
P('vortex','Vortex comes from Latin vortex, “whirlpool,” related to vertere, “to turn”; it names a rapidly rotating flow of air or liquid.',C('vortex.s1','fluid motion','Leaves circled in the small vortex that formed above the drain as the water emptied.','水排空时，树叶在排水口上方形成的小漩涡里打转。','a vortex of water/air; form a vortex','名词，指快速旋转的液体或气流。','The leaves rotate around the moving water.','漩涡'),M('The water formed a vortex and flowed in a perfectly straight line without turning.','The water formed a current and flowed in a perfectly straight line without turning.','A vortex rotates; a straight nonrotating flow is a current.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened to the leaves?','They circled in rotating water','They stayed on a dry shelf','They moved in a straight line without turning','A vortex is a rotating flow.','context'),Q(1,'A vortex is best described as…','a whirling flow of air or liquid','a fixed block of ice','a unit of electric potential','The word names swirling motion.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which collocation is natural?','a vortex of air','a vortex of voltage','a vote of water','Vortex commonly refers to rotating air or liquid.','collocation'),Q(1,'The Latin source of vortex is associated with…','a whirlpool and turning','a written promise','a small bird','The word’s historical sense is a whirlpool.','word-formation')]);
P('vote','Vote is from Latin votum, “wish, promise, or solemn pledge”; it can mean choosing formally, reaching a group decision, or the recorded choice/right.',[C('vote.s1','election','Residents will vote for a mayor at the polling station on Tuesday.','居民将在周二投票站选举市长。','vote for/against a candidate; vote in an election','动词，指通过正式投票表达选择。','They make a formal choice among candidates.','投票'),C('vote.s2','decision','The committee voted to postpone the meeting until the budget was ready.','委员会投票决定把会议推迟到预算准备好以后。','vote to do something; vote on a proposal','动词，指以投票方式作出集体决定。','The group decides by voting.','表决'),C('vote.s3','ballot/right','Her vote was counted after she marked one name on the ballot.','她在选票上标出一个名字后，她的选票被计入。','cast/count a vote; have the right to vote','名词，指一次投票、投票结果或投票权。','The marked choice is one vote.','选票；投票权')],M('The residents voted for a mayor by refusing to mark or submit any ballot.','The residents abstained from voting by refusing to mark or submit any ballot.','A person who submits no ballot has not voted.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What will residents do on Tuesday?','Choose a mayor by ballot','Measure a circuit’s voltage','Attend a sea voyage','Sense 1 is formal choice in an election.','context'),Q(2,'What did the committee decide?','Postpone the meeting','Count the residents’ votes twice','Elect a mayor','Sense 2 describes a group decision by vote.','context'),Q(3,'What happened to her vote?','It was counted after she marked the ballot','It was used to measure the room','It was mailed as a travel visa','Sense 3 can mean a recorded ballot.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','vote on a proposal','vote a proposal to','vote for to a proposal','English uses vote on when deciding a question.','grammar')]);
P('vote in','Vote in combines vote with the particle in and means elect someone to office or approve something through a ballot.',[C('vote in.s1','election','The district voted in a new council member after the incumbent announced her retirement.','现任议员宣布退休后，该选区投票选出了一位新的议员。','vote someone in; vote in a candidate','动词短语，指通过投票选某人担任职位。','The ballot brings the candidate into office.','投票选出'),C('vote in.s2','approval','The club voted in the revised rules after members discussed each change.','会员逐项讨论每项修改后，俱乐部投票通过了修订后的规则。','vote in a motion/rule; vote something in','动词短语，指通过投票批准某项提案或规则。','The vote makes the proposed rules official.','投票通过')],M('The club voted in the revised rules by rejecting them in the final ballot.','The club voted down the revised rules by rejecting them in the final ballot.','Rejecting a proposal is voting it down, not voting it in.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Who entered office after the district’s vote?','A new council member','The retiring incumbent by default','A visiting tourist','Sense 1 means elect someone to a position.','context'),Q(2,'What happened to the revised rules?','Members approved them by ballot','Members rejected them without a vote','They became travel documents','Sense 2 means approve through a vote.','context'),Q(1,'What does “vote someone in” mean?','Elect that person to a position','Ask the person to leave office','Record the person’s address','The particle in signals entry into office.','meaning'),Q(2,'If members vote a motion in, they…','approve it','cancel the ballot','send it to a different club','The phrase means formally accept a proposal.','meaning')]);
P('voter','Voter is formed from vote + -er and names a person who is eligible to vote or who casts a ballot.',[C('voter.s1','eligibility','Every registered voter received a notice explaining where to cast a ballot.','每位登记选民都收到了一份说明投票地点的通知。','registered/eligible voter; voter registration','名词，指有资格参加选举的人。','The notice is sent to someone entitled to vote.','选民'),C('voter.s2','participation','A voter placed her completed ballot in the sealed box before leaving the polling station.','一位选民在离开投票站前把填好的选票放进了密封箱。','voter turnout; a first-time voter','名词，指实际投票的人。','She personally casts a ballot.','投票者')],M('The voter cast a ballot even though he was not allowed to take part in the election.','The observer watched the ballot count but did not vote.','A person not allowed to vote cannot properly be described as a voter in that election.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did each registered voter receive a notice?','They were eligible to cast a ballot','They were selected to count voltages','They had applied for a visa','Sense 1 is a person entitled to vote.','context'),Q(2,'What did the woman do at the polling station?','Placed her completed ballot in the box','Counted votes from home','Registered a new club rule','Sense 2 refers to someone who actually votes.','context'),Q(1,'A first-time voter is someone who…','is voting in an election for the first time','has never been allowed to vote','is counting electric current','The compound describes voting experience.','meaning'),Q(1,'Voter is formed from…','vote + -er','vowel + -er','vow + -age','The suffix -er names a person who performs the action.','word-formation')]);
P('voting','Voting is the -ing form of vote and names the act of casting ballots or having the right to do so.',[C('voting.s1','election','Voting began at seven in the morning, and the first results were announced that night.','投票于早上七点开始，首批结果当晚公布。','voting begins; voting process; voting booth','名词，指选举中投票的行为或过程。','People cast their ballots during this process.','投票'),C('voting.s2','rights','The constitution protects voting rights for citizens who meet the age requirement.','宪法保护符合年龄要求的公民的投票权。','voting rights; voting age','名词作定语，指投票的权利或资格。','The phrase concerns the right to cast a ballot.','投票权')],M('Voting rights were protected by preventing eligible citizens from casting ballots.','Voting rights were restricted when eligible citizens were prevented from casting ballots.','Preventing eligible people from voting restricts their rights rather than protecting them.','meaning'),[Q(1,'When did voting begin?','At seven in the morning','After the final results were announced','Only the following year','Sense 1 names the ballot-casting process.','context'),Q(2,'What does “voting rights” refer to?','The right to cast a ballot','The right to measure electric current','A document for crossing a border','Sense 2 concerns eligibility and rights.','context'),Q(1,'In “Voting began at seven,” voting is…','a noun naming an activity','an adjective describing a person','a past-tense verb','The subject of began is the activity noun.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','voting booth','votingly booth','booth voteable','Voting commonly modifies booth and rights.','collocation')]);
P('voucher','Voucher comes from Anglo-French and Old French words meaning “call” or “summon”; it now names proof of payment or a document exchangeable for goods or services.',[C('voucher.s1','payment','Keep the taxi voucher because the finance office requires proof of the trip’s cost.','请保留出租车收据凭证，因为财务办公室需要这次行程费用的证明。','expense/payment voucher; redeem a voucher','名词，指证明已付款或可报销金额的凭证。','The paper documents the expense.','凭证'),C('voucher.s2','exchange','The festival voucher can be exchanged for one meal at any food stall.','这张节庆代金券可在任意一个餐摊兑换一份餐食。','gift/meal voucher; voucher for services','名词，指可兑换商品或服务的票券。','The holder trades the document for a meal.','代金券')],M('She used the meal voucher to prove the taxi fare she had already paid.','She submitted the taxi receipt to prove the fare she had already paid.','A meal voucher is exchangeable for food, not proof of a taxi payment.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why should the traveler keep the taxi voucher?','It proves the trip’s cost','It gives a free meal at the festival','It records an election choice','Sense 1 is a payment or expense document.','context'),Q(2,'What can the festival voucher buy?','One meal at a food stall','A taxi fare refund','A passport stamp','Sense 2 is an exchangeable ticket.','context'),Q(1,'A gift voucher is usually…','exchanged for goods or services','used to measure voltage','a person’s ballot','The document carries exchange value.','meaning'),Q(1,'Voucher is historically related to a French verb meaning…','to call or summon','to turn into a whirlpool','to sing a vowel','The word’s older legal sense involved calling someone to vouch.','word-formation')]);
P('vow','Vow is from Latin votum, “a solemn promise or dedication”; it functions as both a serious promise and the act of making one.',[C('vow.s1','promise noun','The climber made a vow to return every summer and maintain the trail markers.','登山者立誓每年夏天都回来维护步道标记。','make/take a vow; a vow to do something','名词，指郑重作出的承诺。','The climber makes a serious promise.','誓言'),C('vow.s2','promise verb','Before the hearing, the witness vowed to tell the truth and answer every question.','听证会前，证人郑重承诺会说实话并回答每个问题。','vow to do something; vow that…','动词，指郑重承诺做某事或某事属实。','The witness makes a firm promise.','发誓')],M('The witness vowed to conceal the truth but promised to answer every question honestly.','The witness vowed to tell the truth and answer every question honestly.','The sentence contradicts itself; a vow to conceal is not a promise to tell the truth.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the climber promise?','To return yearly and maintain the markers','To close the trail permanently','To avoid the mountains','Sense 1 is a serious promise.','context'),Q(2,'What did the witness vow to do?','Tell the truth and answer questions','Cancel the hearing','Refuse to speak','Sense 2 uses vow as a verb meaning promise solemnly.','context'),Q(1,'Which collocation is standard?','make a vow','do a vow at someone','vow to a promise','English commonly uses make or take a vow.','collocation'),Q(2,'In “She vowed that she would return,” vowed is…','a verb meaning promised solemnly','a noun meaning a ballot','an adjective meaning noisy','The clause after vowed gives the promise.','grammar')]);
P('vowel','Vowel came through French from Latin vocalis, “of the voice”; it names a speech sound made without the mouth blocking the airflow, and its written letter.',C('vowel.s1','phonetics','In the word “team,” the letters ea represent a vowel sound.','在单词 team 中，字母组合 ea 表示一个元音。','vowel sound; vowel letter; long/short vowel','名词，指元音语音或表示元音的字母。','The sound is produced without a complete blockage of airflow.','元音'),M('The teacher called the open sound in “team” a consonant because the airflow was unblocked.','The teacher called the open sound in “team” a vowel because the airflow was unblocked.','A vowel is produced without the airflow being blocked by the mouth.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What do the letters ea represent in “team”?','A vowel sound','A punctuation mark','A number','The context identifies the sound as a vowel.','context'),Q(1,'A vowel sound is made…','without a complete blockage of airflow','only by closing the lips completely','with the tongue sealing the throat','Vowels are articulated with an open vocal tract.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','a vowel sound','a vowelly sound','sound of vowelly','Vowel is the adjective-like noun modifier in this phrase.','collocation'),Q(1,'The Latin source vocalis relates to…','the voice','a ballot','a winding current','Vocalis means “of the voice.”','word-formation')]);
P('voyage','Voyage came through Old French from Late Latin viaticum, “a journey”; it can mean a long trip, especially by sea, a figurative journey, or the act of traveling by sea.',[C('voyage.s1','sea travel','The research ship began its voyage across the Pacific after the storm passed.','风暴过后，科考船开始了横渡太平洋的航行。','go on a voyage; a voyage across the sea','名词，指长途旅行，尤指海上航行。','The ship makes a long journey over water.','航行'),C('voyage.s2','figurative journey','Her memoir describes the emotional voyage from grief to acceptance.','她的回忆录讲述了从悲伤走向接纳的心路历程。','a voyage of discovery; an emotional voyage','比喻指一段经历或探索过程。','The journey is personal rather than physical.','历程'),C('voyage.s3','travel verb','The small boat voyaged from island to island, carrying mail and supplies.','这艘小船往返于各个岛屿之间，运送邮件和物资。','voyage across/through; voyage to a place','动词，指乘船长途航行。','The boat travels by sea between islands.','航行')],M('The research ship began a voyage across the Pacific by walking overland on foot.','The research ship began a voyage across the Pacific by sailing over the ocean.','A ship’s voyage across the Pacific is a sea journey, not a walk overland.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where was the research ship traveling?','Across the Pacific','Across a classroom','Between two city bus stops','Sense 1 is a long sea journey.','context'),Q(2,'What kind of voyage does the memoir describe?','An emotional journey from grief to acceptance','A cargo trip between islands','A trip to measure voltage','Sense 2 is figurative.','context'),Q(3,'What did the small boat do?','Traveled from island to island','Stayed anchored in one harbor','Crossed the desert on foot','Sense 3 uses voyage as a verb for sea travel.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a voyage across the ocean','a voyage for the oceanly','a voyal journey','Voyage is a noun for a journey, often by sea.','collocation')]);
P('voyager','Voyager comes from Old French voyagier, “one who travels,” from voyage; it names someone who makes a journey, especially a long one.',C('voyager.s1','exploration','The voyager kept a careful log of each island reached during the long expedition.','这位航海旅行者仔细记录了长途探险中到达的每座岛屿。','a space/ocean voyager; voyager on an expedition','名词，指进行长途旅行或探索的人。','The person travels from place to place on an expedition.','旅行者'),M('The voyager stayed at home and never traveled anywhere during the expedition.','The researcher stayed at home and never traveled anywhere during the expedition.','A voyager is someone who undertakes a journey.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the voyager record?','Each island reached on the expedition','The daily voltage of a room','Votes cast in a local election','A voyager travels and can document the journey.','context'),Q(1,'A voyager is…','a person who makes a journey','a document used as a meal coupon','a device that measures current','The noun refers to a traveler.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a space voyager','a voyager voltage','a voyageable person only','Voyager names a traveler and can modify a field such as space.','collocation'),Q(1,'Voyager is formed from…','voyage + -er','vowel + -er','vote + -age','The suffix -er makes a person noun from voyage.','word-formation')]);
P('vs','Vs is an abbreviation of Latin versus, “against”; it is used between opponents’ names and in legal case titles.',[C('vs.s1','competition','The final is Northside vs Easton, so both teams will compete for the championship.','决赛是 Northside 对 Easton，两队将争夺冠军。','Team A vs Team B; the match is X vs Y','缩写，表示两方在比赛或比较中对阵。','The two teams are opponents.','对；对阵'),C('vs.s2','law','The court listed the case as Rivera vs State in the morning docket.','法院在上午的案件表中将此案列为 Rivera 诉州政府。','A vs B; case of X vs Y','法律案件标题中的缩写，标明诉讼双方。','The names identify the opposing parties.','诉')],M('The case title “Rivera vs State” means the two parties are cooperating as teammates.','The case title “Rivera vs State” identifies the opposing parties in the lawsuit.','In a case title, vs marks the parties on opposing sides.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does Northside vs Easton announce?','A championship match between the teams','A joint training session','A court ruling','Sense 1 marks opposing competitors.','context'),Q(2,'Who are the parties in Rivera vs State?','Rivera and the state as opposing lawsuit parties','Two teammates on the same side','A team and its coach','Sense 2 appears in case titles.','context'),Q(1,'Vs is short for the Latin word…','versus','vowel','votum','The abbreviation preserves versus, meaning against.','word-formation'),Q(1,'Which use is standard?','The match is Lions vs Tigers.','The match is versusly Lions Tigers.','The match is vss Lions and Tigers.','Vs is written between the names of opponents.','grammar')]);
P('vulcanization','Vulcanization is formed from Vulcan, the Roman god of fire, + -ization; it is the heat-and-sulfur process that strengthens rubber.',C('vulcanization.s1','materials science','Vulcanization made the rubber tire tougher and less likely to soften in summer heat.','硫化处理使橡胶轮胎更坚韧，也不易在夏季高温下软化。','rubber vulcanization; process of vulcanization','名词，指通常用硫和热处理橡胶，使其更耐用的过程。','The treated rubber becomes stronger and more heat-resistant.','硫化'),M('Vulcanization weakened the rubber tire by removing the treatment that made it durable.','Untreated rubber remained less durable than the tire after vulcanization.','Vulcanization is the strengthening treatment, not the removal of it.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What effect did vulcanization have on the tire?','It made the rubber tougher','It turned the rubber into paper','It made the tire softer in summer','The context identifies vulcanization as a strengthening treatment.','context'),Q(1,'Vulcanization is a process applied especially to…','rubber','glass lenses','voting ballots','The word names a rubber treatment.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','rubber vulcanization','vulcanization of ballots','voltage vulcanization','The process concerns treating rubber.','collocation'),Q(1,'The name vulcanization refers to Vulcan, the Roman god of…','fire','the sea','writing','The process uses heat, linking its name to the fire god.','word-formation')]);
P('vulgar','Vulgar comes from Latin vulgaris, “of the common people”; it can mean crude or offensive, or showy in a way that displays poor taste.',[C('vulgar.s1','language','The host apologized after a vulgar joke offended several guests at the formal dinner.','一则粗俗笑话冒犯了正式晚宴上的几位客人，主人随后道歉。','vulgar language/joke; vulgar expression','形容言语粗俗、冒犯或不雅。','The joke is offensive in the setting.','粗俗的'),C('vulgar.s2','taste','Gold lettering covered every surface of the room, giving the decoration a vulgar look.','房间的每个表面都贴满金色字样，使装饰显得俗气。','vulgar display/taste; look vulgar','形容装饰炫耀、俗气，显示品味欠佳。','The excessive display looks tasteless.','俗气的')],M('The vulgar joke was polite and suitable for every formal ceremony.','The tactful joke was polite and suitable for the formal ceremony.','A vulgar joke is crude or offensive, not tactful and ceremonially appropriate.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the host apologize?','The joke offended guests','The room had no decorations','The dinner was informal','Sense 1 describes crude or offensive speech.','context'),Q(2,'Why did the room look vulgar?','It was covered in excessive gold lettering','It had a simple and restrained design','It was empty','Sense 2 concerns showy poor taste.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a vulgar joke','a vulgarly joke','a joke vulgarity','Vulgar is an adjective modifying joke.','grammar'),Q(1,'The Latin source vulgaris referred to…','the common people','electrical potential','a sea journey','The word originally meant “of the common people.”','word-formation')]);
P('vulgarity','Vulgarity is formed from vulgar + -ity and means crude or offensive behavior, language, or a lack of refinement.',[C('vulgarity.s1','manners','The reviewer criticized the vulgarity of the insults, not the play’s difficult subject.','评论者批评的是那些侮辱性言辞的粗俗，而不是戏剧艰深的主题。','language/act of vulgarity; avoid vulgarity','名词，指粗俗、低级或冒犯性的言行，也可指缺少雅致。','The insults are crude and offensive.','粗俗')],M('The vulgarity of the insult showed refined manners and considerate language.','The courtesy of the remark showed refined manners and considerate language.','Vulgarity means crude or offensive expression, the opposite of courtesy.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the reviewer criticize?','The crude insults','The difficult subject alone','The stage lighting','Vulgarity refers to offensive language here.','context'),Q(1,'Vulgarity is…','crude or offensive behavior or language','a measure of electrical current','an official promise','The noun names the quality of being vulgar.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the vulgarity of the insults','the vulgarityly insults','insults vulgarity to','The phrase uses of to identify what is vulgar.','grammar'),Q(1,'Vulgarity is formed from…','vulgar + -ity','vulture + -ity','vowel + -ity','The suffix -ity makes an abstract quality noun.','word-formation')]);
P('vulnerability','Vulnerability is vulnerable + -ity; it names the state of being easily harmed or a weakness that can be exploited.',[C('vulnerability.s1','personal safety','The shelter’s vulnerability to flooding became clear when rainwater entered through the low doorway.','雨水从低矮的门口涌入后，避难所易受洪水侵袭的弱点显露出来。','vulnerability to attack/disease; personal vulnerability','名词，指容易受伤、受损或遭受攻击的状态。','The building is easily harmed by flooding.','脆弱性'),C('vulnerability.s2','security','The audit found a vulnerability in the login system that could let an attacker steal passwords.','审计发现登录系统有一个漏洞，攻击者可能借此窃取密码。','security/software vulnerability; exploit a vulnerability','名词，指可被利用的薄弱环节或漏洞。','The weakness can be exploited by an attacker.','漏洞')],M('The audit found no vulnerability, but attackers could easily exploit a weak login flaw.','The audit found a vulnerability because attackers could exploit the weak login flaw.','An exploitable flaw is precisely a vulnerability.','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the shelter’s vulnerability become clear?','Floodwater entered through a low doorway','The shelter resisted every storm','The building gained an extra floor','Sense 1 is susceptibility to harm.','context'),Q(2,'What could an attacker exploit?','A flaw in the login system','A sealed flood door','A voting right','Sense 2 means an exploitable weakness.','context'),Q(1,'A vulnerability in software is…','a weakness that can be exploited','a guaranteed security improvement','a paper travel permit','The term names a security weakness.','meaning'),Q(1,'Vulnerability is formed from…','vulnerable + -ity','vulgar + -ity','visible + -ity','The suffix creates a noun for a state or quality.','word-formation')]);
P('vulnerable','Vulnerable came through Late Latin vulnerabilis, “capable of being wounded,” from Latin vulnerare, “to wound”; it can mean easily harmed or open to attack.',[C('vulnerable.s1','susceptibility','Young seedlings are vulnerable to frost, so the gardener covers them on cold nights.','幼苗容易受霜冻伤害，因此园丁在寒冷的夜晚给它们盖上遮护物。','vulnerable to disease/attack; emotionally vulnerable','形容容易受到伤害或影响。','Frost can harm the seedlings easily.','易受伤害的'),C('vulnerable.s2','exposure','The website remained vulnerable to attacks until the company installed the security update.','在公司安装安全更新之前，该网站一直容易遭受攻击。','vulnerable to attack; leave a system vulnerable','形容处于容易被攻击或利用的状态。','An attacker can exploit the unpatched system.','易受攻击的')],M('The unpatched website was vulnerable to attack, so hackers could not possibly exploit it.','The unpatched website was secure from attack, so hackers could not exploit it.','If hackers can exploit the weakness, the website is vulnerable rather than secure.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the gardener cover the seedlings?','They were easily harmed by frost','They had already grown into trees','They needed more sunlight at night','Sense 1 means susceptible to harm.','context'),Q(2,'Why was the website vulnerable?','It lacked a security update','It had no connection to the internet','It had been permanently deleted','Sense 2 is exposure to attack.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is standard?','vulnerable to frost','vulnerable from frost','vulnerable with frostly','Vulnerable is commonly followed by to.','grammar'),Q(1,'The Latin source vulnerare means…','to wound or hurt','to promise solemnly','to turn around','Vulnerable derives from a Latin verb meaning wound.','word-formation')]);
P('vulture','Vulture comes from Latin vultur and names a large bird that feeds on dead animals; figuratively, it can describe someone who profits from others’ trouble.',[C('vulture.s1','bird','A vulture circled above the dry plain, searching for a carcass left by predators.','一只秃鹫在干旱的平原上盘旋，寻找被捕食者留下的尸体。','a vulture feeds on carrion; vulture population','名词，指以腐肉为食的大型鸟类。','The bird searches for an animal carcass.','秃鹫'),C('vulture.s1','figurative','The columnist called the fraudster a vulture for exploiting families after the storm.','专栏作者称那名骗子是秃鹫，因为他在风暴后趁灾民困境牟利。','a financial vulture; vultures prey on the vulnerable','比喻指趁他人遭难而牟利的人。','The person takes advantage of people in crisis.','趁人之危者')],M('The vulture fed on flowers and never approached dead animals on the plain.','The vulture fed on carrion and circled above the plain.','Vultures are scavengers that feed on dead animals.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the bird searching for?','A carcass left by predators','A ballot box','A freshwater fish it had caught alive','Sense 1 is the scavenging bird.','context'),Q(1,'Why did the columnist call the fraudster a vulture?','He profited from families’ hardship','He protected families from scams','He worked as a bird researcher','Sense 2 is a person who exploits others in trouble.','context'),Q(1,'A vulture typically feeds on…','carrion','fresh leaves only','electric current','The bird is a scavenger.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a vulture circling above a carcass','a vulture measuring voltage','a vulture voting in a council','The phrase reflects the bird’s feeding behavior.','collocation')]);
P('wad','Wad is a word of uncertain origin; it names a soft lump or bundle of material, such as paper or cotton, and can also mean a thick bundle of money.',[C('wad.s1','bundle','He stuffed a wad of cotton into the small gap to stop the draft from coming through.','他把一团棉花塞进小缝里，挡住漏进来的冷风。','a wad of paper/cotton; a wad of cash','名词，指松软材料团成的一团，也可指一叠钞票。','The cotton is pressed into a soft lump.','团；一叠')],M('She used a wad of cotton by spreading one loose fiber across the entire doorway.','She used a sheet of cotton to cover the entire doorway.','A wad is a compact bundle, not a single loose fiber.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did he put in the gap?','A compact lump of cotton','A metal voltmeter','A travel voucher','The cotton forms a wad that fills the small gap.','context'),Q(1,'A wad of cash is…','a thick bundle of banknotes','one loose coin','a paper ballot','Wad can describe a bundle of money.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is standard?','a wad of paper','a wad at paper','wadly paper','Wad is followed by of before the material.','grammar'),Q(1,'What is known about the history of wad?','Its origin is uncertain','It certainly comes from Latin votum','It was named after the Roman fire god','The etymology is not securely established.','word-formation')]);
P('wade','Wade comes from Old English wadan, “to go or advance”; it means to walk through shallow water or figuratively work through something long and difficult.',[C('wade.s1','water','We waded across the shallow stream because the footbridge had washed away.','人行桥被冲毁后，我们蹚过了那条浅溪。','wade through/across water; wade into the river','动词，指涉水行走。','They walk through water rather than swim.','蹚水'),C('wade.s2','reading','The editor had to wade through hundreds of pages of testimony before writing the report.','编辑在撰写报告前不得不费力读完数百页证词。','wade through paperwork/text; wade through a report','比喻费力处理或阅读大量枯燥材料。','The editor works through a long text with effort.','费力处理'),C('wade.s3','activity','The wade across the flooded lane took nearly ten minutes.','蹚过被淹小路的过程花了将近十分钟。','a wade through water; take a wade','名词，指涉水行走的一段过程。','The phrase names the act of walking through water.','涉水行走')],M('The hikers waded across the deep lake by flying above it without entering the water.','The hikers crossed the deep lake by boat without entering the water.','To wade is to walk through water, not fly over it.','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the group wade across the stream?','The footbridge had washed away','The water was too deep to see','They wanted to fly across','Sense 1 means walk through shallow water.','context'),Q(2,'What did the editor have to work through?','Hundreds of pages of testimony','A short text message','A flooded river','Sense 2 is a figurative, effortful reading.','context'),Q(3,'How long did the wade take?','Nearly ten minutes','No time because it was a book','Several weeks at sea','Sense 3 is the activity of walking through water.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','wade through paperwork','wade over paperworkly','wade paperwork at through','Wade through is the standard construction for going through material.','collocation')]);
P('wag','Wag is from Old English wagian and related Germanic forms for moving back and forth; it can mean move a tail or finger, one such movement, or a joking person.',[C('wag.s1','movement','The dog began to wag its tail when its owner opened the garden gate.','主人打开花园门时，狗开始摇尾巴。','wag one’s tail/finger; wag back and forth','动词，指使身体部位来回摆动。','The tail moves alternately from side to side.','摇摆'),C('wag.s2','single motion','She gave one wag of her finger to warn the children away from the hot stove.','她摇了一下手指，提醒孩子们远离热炉子。','a wag of the head/tail; one wag','名词，指一次来回摆动。','The word counts one movement.','一次摇摆'),C('wag.s3','humorous person','The office wag left a harmless cartoon on the noticeboard to make everyone laugh.','办公室里的幽默人物在公告板上贴了一幅无伤大雅的漫画，逗大家发笑。','an office wag; a witty wag','名词，指爱开玩笑、诙谐的人。','The person is known for humor.','诙谐的人')],M('The dog wagged its tail by holding it perfectly still while greeting its owner.','The dog held its tail still while greeting its owner.','Wag means move back and forth, so a still tail is not wagging.','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the dog do when the gate opened?','Moved its tail from side to side','Held its tail completely still','Barked at a volleyball','Sense 1 is the movement verb.','context'),Q(2,'What did one wag of her finger do?','Warn the children away','Measure the room’s voltage','Approve the new rules','Sense 2 names a single movement.','context'),Q(3,'Why was the office employee called a wag?','He was known for making people laugh','He measured the water level','He refused to move his finger','Sense 3 is a humorous person.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','wag its tail','wag to its tail','tail wagly it','Wag takes the moving body part as its object.','grammar')]);
})(typeof window!=='undefined'?window:globalThis);
